Text":"All of the above","explanation":"Dopamine-depleting medicines such as reserpine and dopamine receptor blockers such as haloperidol and chlorpromazine can oppose levodopa's antiparkinsonian benefits.","optionReasons":{"D":"Dopamine-depleting medicines such as reserpine and dopamine receptor blockers such as haloperidol and chlorpromazine can oppose levodopa's antiparkinsonian benefits."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"45373e587b965087228e685eebafd431d4a631ebf9d941f5a1ad87c70a0e6894"},"q-e8637f0fb389":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Monoamine oxydase A inhibitors","explanation":"Combining levodopa with nonselective or MAO-A inhibitors can markedly raise catecholamine availability and precipitate severe hypertension; selective MAO-B inhibitors require separate assessment.","optionReasons":{"B":"Combining levodopa with nonselective or MAO-A inhibitors can markedly raise catecholamine availability and precipitate severe hypertension; selective MAO-B inhibitors require separate assessment."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e2493e3f87e1e86247efe323b740cd3392eb83861c9107cde0892ff591315a57"},"q-1a6f852d81eb":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Bromocriptine","explanation":"Bromocriptine is a dopamine D2 receptor agonist that can improve parkinsonian motor symptoms and reduce prolactin secretion.","optionReasons":{"C":"Bromocriptine is a dopamine D2 receptor agonist that can improve parkinsonian motor symptoms and reduce prolactin secretion."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ab06ae12261504581b91d35aa8cf91089580e30778f858d72aa46ed1bb991c7b"},"q-96ecdb5e3057":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Bromocriptine","explanation":"Bromocriptine activates dopamine D2 receptors on pituitary lactotrophs, suppressing prolactin release and treating selected hyperprolactinemia cases.","optionReasons":{"B":"Bromocriptine activates dopamine D2 receptors on pituitary lactotrophs, suppressing prolactin release and treating selected hyperprolactinemia cases."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"20fa76fd30ed86a5d8ae9f6dac919319356be19112f245efa46d280406b7024c"},"q-7cced67305cc":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Selegiline","explanation":"Selegiline preferentially inhibits monoamine oxidase B at usual doses and slows dopamine metabolism in the brain.","optionReasons":{"D":"Selegiline preferentially inhibits monoamine oxidase B at usual doses and slows dopamine metabolism in the brain."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3c38f4dd0d014c69a220d1ed4b45094e71c86c42557625708724d67de68e809a"},"q-66452714b003":{"correct":"C","answerText":"MAO-A metabolizes norepinephrine and serotonin; MAO-B metabolizes dopamine","explanation":"MAO-A preferentially metabolizes serotonin and norepinephrine, whereas MAO-B participates prominently in dopamine metabolism; the distinction is not absolute because both can metabolize dopamine.","optionReasons":{"C":"MAO-A preferentially metabolizes serotonin and norepinephrine, whereas MAO-B participates prominently in dopamine metabolism; the distinction is not absolute because both can metabolize dopamine."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"392e94537bb7a083210b1a5ce8179d6cc7bad0a91cc4795748ac68c471da16a0"},"q-f210c240d6f2":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Hypertensive emergency","explanation":"Nonselective monoamine oxidase inhibition during levodopa therapy can trigger excessive catecholamine effects, including hypertensive crises.","optionReasons":{"B":"Nonselective monoamine oxidase inhibition during levodopa therapy can trigger excessive catecholamine effects, including hypertensive crises."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e8c9243ca5805f729b13d22c310fdbaa9d2f3c7fdae5b6657dee819d99f2454c"},"q-939af48d9a08":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Amantadine","explanation":"Amantadine is an antiviral agent historically used against influenza A and is also used to treat selected symptoms and dyskinesias in Parkinson disease.","optionReasons":{"D":"Amantadine is an antiviral agent historically used against influenza A and is also used to treat selected symptoms and dyskinesias in Parkinson disease."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"931c32e8c0754c60a249cd8ee52ea8d6d64abb914d3adc40917b51a742e9e101"},"q-4f0f288baeef":{"correct":"E","answerText":"alcoholism","explanation":"Structural heart disease, damaged endocardium, intravascular catheters and injection-drug exposure increase endocarditis risk, whereas alcoholism alone is not a standard direct structural predisposing condition.","optionReasons":{"E":"Structural heart disease, damaged endocardium, intravascular catheters and injection-drug exposure increase endocarditis risk, whereas alcoholism alone is not a standard direct structural predisposing condition."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5e6ba9c5eaca12de6475ebbfdc69eecf69fe7f208503515a91bddd2ed0946260"},"q-81034cece3b1":{"correct":"D","answerText":"hypertension","explanation":"Congenital lesions, rheumatic valve disease, injected drugs and intravascular devices predispose to endocarditis; uncomplicated hypertension is not a typical direct predisposing lesion.","optionReasons":{"D":"Congenital lesions, rheumatic valve disease, injected drugs and intravascular devices predispose to endocarditis; uncomplicated hypertension is not a typical direct predisposing lesion."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"69d236c7a3220df3d411b64c6b551b8bf27597452b3639a596670654a077c9f1"},"q-c875162fa3b9":{"correct":"B","answerText":"infected by virus A and identical at class I MHC loci of the cytotoxic T cells.","explanation":"Cytotoxic CD8 T cells recognize virus-derived peptides displayed on matching MHC class I molecules, so target killing requires appropriate antigen and class-I restriction.","optionReasons":{"B":"Cytotoxic CD8 T cells recognize virus-derived peptides displayed on matching MHC class I molecules, so target killing requires appropriate antigen and class-I restriction."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"de7ab2d7e097aa455db3df261ffa368c530cfc1e3f32ef1e22f6ed214cf197a7"},"q-48c4c97657bf":{"correct":"C","answerText":"inactivation of the drug.","explanation":"A major acquired aminoglycoside-resistance mechanism is enzymatic drug modification by aminoglycoside acetyltransferases, phosphotransferases or nucleotidyltransferases.","optionReasons":{"C":"A major acquired aminoglycoside-resistance mechanism is enzymatic drug modification by aminoglycoside acetyltransferases, phosphotransferases or nucleotidyltransferases."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4a2789e757ca49352dc57e0c61b7b806424a27ec9e0bc0b03f4c15731786f65b"},"q-c376893a6c55":{"correct":"A","answerText":"depolarizing the cell membrane.","explanation":"Daptomycin inserts into bacterial membranes and disrupts membrane potential, rapidly inhibiting essential biosynthetic functions including DNA and RNA synthesis.","optionReasons":{"A":"Daptomycin inserts into bacterial membranes and disrupts membrane potential, rapidly inhibiting essential biosynthetic functions including DNA and RNA synthesis."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ba8c3ad7fe663a532256a956a3a2c0671a91733ed8b05f2fa0ca0f9f4714102e"},"q-78a022963eb3":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Its selectivity for Herpes DNA polymerase","explanation":"Acyclovir has strong selectivity for herpes-infected cells because activation is favored by viral thymidine kinase and its active triphosphate preferentially inhibits viral DNA polymerase.","optionReasons":{"D":"Acyclovir has strong selectivity for herpes-infected cells because activation is favored by viral thymidine kinase and its active triphosphate preferentially inhibits viral DNA polymerase."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"675cc43f508f8af94fd36b924c012c0007c867f3e1cbc6847443e337e54755b1"},"q-73dfbf151faa":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Klebsiella pneumonia","explanation":"Klebsiella pneumoniae is a Gram-negative enteric bacillus; Listeria, the staphylococci and streptococci listed are Gram-positive organisms.","optionReasons":{"D":"Klebsiella pneumoniae is a Gram-negative enteric bacillus; Listeria, the staphylococci and streptococci listed are Gram-positive organisms."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4d383de22840fb7cd07c6dd0ab7a5ad29eaaba059a7d91e45674f86ec8ea2932"},"q-eac56280cdf6":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Bacillus anthracis","explanation":"Bacillus anthracis is a large Gram-positive rod. Staphylococci, neisseriae and moraxellae are coccoid, while Borrelia is a spirochete.","optionReasons":{"C":"Bacillus anthracis is a large Gram-positive rod. Staphylococci, neisseriae and moraxellae are coccoid, while Borrelia is a spirochete."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e82e7c4495c64d03701044527d8b401496a78ddc3942f6209e7a0a9a0f0bcecf"},"q-75dfb65a7996":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Gram-positive rods","explanation":"Listeria monocytogenes is a short Gram-positive, facultatively intracellular rod that can show tumbling motility.","optionReasons":{"E":"Listeria monocytogenes is a short Gram-positive, facultatively intracellular rod that can show tumbling motility."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3c58ae677d7ec0d267ae6953f301aac8d9ffdfce9f360138027402751180252a"},"q-4e4af3940e41":{"correct":"D","answerText":"1,000x","explanation":"A 100-times oil-immersion objective combined with a 10-times ocular lens provides approximately 1,000-times total magnification for bacterial microscopy.","optionReasons":{"D":"A 100-times oil-immersion objective combined with a 10-times ocular lens provides approximately 1,000-times total magnification for bacterial microscopy."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a8393b3cb583b07ab50e7a79a5836876101c3a03d0508a9e7a577b10ce95cad2"},"q-9743d4407eef":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Yellow","explanation":"Mannitol fermentation generates acid and changes phenol-red mannitol salt agar from pink/red toward yellow around positive colonies.","optionReasons":{"D":"Mannitol fermentation generates acid and changes phenol-red mannitol salt agar from pink/red toward yellow around positive colonies."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1d4c55538464695a5a4f782f77d46dc4d487b9c9dd3f2d910b829cdd209f86c5"},"q-3856fa53b274":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Neonatal meningitis","explanation":"Neonatal bacterial meningitis is classically associated with group B Streptococcus and Escherichia coli, not principally Streptococcus pneumoniae.","optionReasons":{"B":"Neonatal bacterial meningitis is classically associated with group B Streptococcus and Escherichia coli, not principally Streptococcus pneumoniae."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fc4cc5f0c596d6291e9bd1583377d4324e745147af3dad938a66ef46c39c8084"},"q-5a2cc0d8850f":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Green","explanation":"Alpha hemolysis is partial red-cell lysis with conversion of hemoglobin pigments, producing a greenish zone around colonies on blood agar.","optionReasons":{"C":"Alpha hemolysis is partial red-cell lysis with conversion of hemoglobin pigments, producing a greenish zone around colonies on blood agar."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1feef18fa89eb746c16572a0e31fc2dc64a53d1a02e0ed0ba29e6a51a38e0e2d"},"q-d534a7de308d":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Staphylococci aureus","explanation":"Staphylococcus aureus is characteristically catalase-positive and coagulase-positive, unlike common coagulase-negative staphylococci or streptococci.","optionReasons":{"C":"Staphylococcus aureus is characteristically catalase-positive and coagulase-positive, unlike common coagulase-negative staphylococci or streptococci."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a5172e447b4bbf1c137ff113a7a57877ad090b69029a74dc4e2e1e6460463c51"},"q-a856ae4348b2":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Enterococcus Lab 3 – Gram-negative Bacteria","explanation":"Enterococcus species are frequently nonhemolytic on blood agar and can be categorized as gamma hemolytic, unlike typical beta-hemolytic pyogenes and agalactiae.","optionReasons":{"E":"Enterococcus species are frequently nonhemolytic on blood agar and can be categorized as gamma hemolytic, unlike typical beta-hemolytic pyogenes and agalactiae."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ab154b7deb6f298443c55bd105b58dae6ebc8ed2fd9e55fb2dfdb2c56561866e"},"q-2d666961bc2f":{"correct":"C","answerText":"P. aeruginosa","explanation":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a non-glucose-fermenting Gram-negative rod that is oxidase-positive, distinguishing it from common enteric fermenters.","optionReasons":{"C":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a non-glucose-fermenting Gram-negative rod that is oxidase-positive, distinguishing it from common enteric fermenters."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7e43a3f319c37763ecc6f26826497b38a0567df67cdd9b28db9deceaa514670f"},"q-9c2ff63b8e80":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Pink","explanation":"Lactose-fermenting organisms acidify MacConkey agar, producing pink to red colonies due to the neutral-red pH indicator.","optionReasons":{"B":"Lactose-fermenting organisms acidify MacConkey agar, producing pink to red colonies due to the neutral-red pH indicator."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1b56992aa92c466c7463a6a823d77e042829294437793968bd08b5d52174ba32"},"q-8bbfa6647255":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Shigella","explanation":"Shigella produces bloody inflammatory diarrhea, is a non-lactose fermenting Gram-negative bacillus and is typically hydrogen-sulfide negative.","optionReasons":{"B":"Shigella produces bloody inflammatory diarrhea, is a non-lactose fermenting Gram-negative bacillus and is typically hydrogen-sulfide negative."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b91128fd5bd8687bccb3d466e2add5199d7f7a78122c65b10fd529413a507716"},"q-62e6e6b2d929":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Type III secretion system Lab 4 – Chocolate Agar and CHO Fermenters","explanation":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa uses a type III secretion apparatus to inject cytotoxic effector proteins into host cells, an important virulence mechanism.","optionReasons":{"E":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa uses a type III secretion apparatus to inject cytotoxic effector proteins into host cells, an important virulence mechanism."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"45f136a227bb4b0755a58b05a4d143334427360e880b75edf67db8e59ef3b2ee"},"q-402bebf7a395":{"correct":"D","answerText":"N. gonorrhea","explanation":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae typically oxidizes glucose but not maltose or sucrose in carbohydrate-use tests, unlike N. meningitidis, which also uses maltose.","optionReasons":{"D":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae typically oxidizes glucose but not maltose or sucrose in carbohydrate-use tests, unlike N. meningitidis, which also uses maltose."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1dad5692f07ed42e47e19d07deabd79c5a0339a0215a2ce5de61a7c3d4c10471"},"q-19845fd2d921":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Pili","explanation":"Type IV pili of Neisseria gonorrhoeae promote epithelial attachment, antigenic variation and tissue colonization; they are major virulence determinants.","optionReasons":{"C":"Type IV pili of Neisseria gonorrhoeae promote epithelial attachment, antigenic variation and tissue colonization; they are major virulence determinants."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"423c4ee92838e32c9dec85c42477554cfa4559e63c90dabf7054ed17bcd65275"},"q-828f8e39ec4c":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Capsule","explanation":"The polyribosylribitol phosphate capsule of encapsulated Haemophilus influenzae type b is a major antiphagocytic virulence determinant associated with invasive disease.","optionReasons":{"A":"The polyribosylribitol phosphate capsule of encapsulated Haemophilus influenzae type b is a major antiphagocytic virulence determinant associated with invasive disease."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b62653860ff111fda107445547d3498a4cea301b3866f0b5424b6169b332bc0a"},"q-faefd688a050":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Viruses","explanation":"Viruses are generally much smaller than bacteria, fungi and multicellular parasites, often requiring electron microscopy for direct visualization.","optionReasons":{"A":"Viruses are generally much smaller than bacteria, fungi and multicellular parasites, often requiring electron microscopy for direct visualization."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1c45ab0b1c481c61d8553f33647ba7a63466142de3994c7083e814e341f3c8df"},"q-b0d6d7d6f334":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Prokaryotic; Eukaryotic","explanation":"Bacteria are prokaryotes lacking a membrane-bound nucleus, whereas fungi are eukaryotic organisms with nuclei and other membrane-bound organelles.","optionReasons":{"B":"Bacteria are prokaryotes lacking a membrane-bound nucleus, whereas fungi are eukaryotic organisms with nuclei and other membrane-bound organelles."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3d22f881c9f9553704a2030b5f7069482175ee17a6d307d86852a68230e9c546"},"q-3cd4a20a2d26":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Malaria","explanation":"Malaria is caused by the protozoan Plasmodium rather than by a virus. Ebola disease and rabies are viral; the other labels are broad syndromes.","optionReasons":{"D":"Malaria is caused by the protozoan Plasmodium rather than by a virus. Ebola disease and rabies are viral; the other labels are broad syndromes."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"15d4fea3a954f814bb2cb8acdc6039da8c81cd907a0a5961f16547fc619c7d8b"},"q-59d6fce12418":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Attaching to P-site during translation allowing for 70S assembly","explanation":"Bacterial initiator N-formylmethionyl tRNA recognizes the start codon in the ribosomal P site and helps assemble the initiation complex before elongation.","optionReasons":{"C":"Bacterial initiator N-formylmethionyl tRNA recognizes the start codon in the ribosomal P site and helps assemble the initiation complex before elongation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5c72351f0bf31c853995300ccb477f0eda8ce4be8df94b13d362582a961543cb"},"q-4f6a18535263":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Transformation","explanation":"Transformation refers to uptake of extracellular naked DNA and genetic incorporation or maintenance by a competent bacterial cell.","optionReasons":{"B":"Transformation refers to uptake of extracellular naked DNA and genetic incorporation or maintenance by a competent bacterial cell."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8fd2daefdd3b1fd7e3c723e1be9f5147276fde42efa7bc8115c07d72f16a3c92"},"q-2c92f7ce00bf":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Conjugation","explanation":"Conjugation transfers genetic material through direct bacterial cell contact, commonly mediated by conjugative pili or mating bridges.","optionReasons":{"A":"Conjugation transfers genetic material through direct bacterial cell contact, commonly mediated by conjugative pili or mating bridges."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3dc4d13e08a4b60bf71351cc3e7d9de0c225c60bff0c9dc77674ae755a4c5941"},"q-c8bee8ebe530":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Integrates into the host without killing the host","explanation":"A lysogen harbors a temperate bacteriophage genome as a prophage without immediate host-cell lysis; induction can later activate a lytic cycle.","optionReasons":{"D":"A lysogen harbors a temperate bacteriophage genome as a prophage without immediate host-cell lysis; induction can later activate a lytic cycle."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9043bd4da2d5733a45ef9ddfefaa88e5c6b97e06900aa23c71e105ec87c333a8"},"q-4b2cb2910568":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Viruses are living organisms","explanation":"Viruses are obligate intracellular genetic parasites that lack independent cellular metabolism and are generally not classified as living cellular organisms.","optionReasons":{"E":"Viruses are obligate intracellular genetic parasites that lack independent cellular metabolism and are generally not classified as living cellular organisms."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f92d36f13ba4843cf3908e31c1515ebdbae36797a80d573e2d5a8bfbb2655e01"},"q-1ce8fb370bcd":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Color","explanation":"Virus classification considers genome, structure and physicochemical or biological properties; color is not a standard taxonomic criterion.","optionReasons":{"B":"Virus classification considers genome, structure and physicochemical or biological properties; color is not a standard taxonomic criterion."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e1b99c27182630284c5562a5211e5e60cd66aa12f2e7b295a3e2ccacaae63cd1"},"q-33304c30eba4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Virion","explanation":"A virion is a complete extracellular virus particle containing a nucleic acid genome in a protective capsid, with an envelope in some viral families.","optionReasons":{"B":"A virion is a complete extracellular virus particle containing a nucleic acid genome in a protective capsid, with an envelope in some viral families."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d01ced0881344d0be696a228859e74c81928ef3a500952b4565fe676bd2b95d7"},"q-0777c9b5b180":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Like bunyaviruses, it does not have matrix proteins","explanation":"Influenza A is a segmented negative-sense RNA virus bearing HA and NA glycoproteins and matrix proteins including M1 and M2.","optionReasons":{"E":"Influenza A is a segmented negative-sense RNA virus bearing HA and NA glycoproteins and matrix proteins including M1 and M2."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6220e558544c179c41a12b074b24ad3dc5b13976f1809d8d1741a64b37c9e394"},"q-335ef533e2fa":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Uncoating","explanation":"Following attachment and cell penetration, many viruses undergo uncoating to make the genome available for transcription or replication.","optionReasons":{"B":"Following attachment and cell penetration, many viruses undergo uncoating to make the genome available for transcription or replication."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d642ef393f3b9a45be430e27a3e74f4250bcfbec90229df864d4cef453a7a99c"},"q-01c1fe7fea70":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Eclipse period","explanation":"The eclipse period is the interval after cell entry during which infectious progeny virions cannot yet be recovered from the infected cell.","optionReasons":{"C":"The eclipse period is the interval after cell entry during which infectious progeny virions cannot yet be recovered from the infected cell."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7df69801f51aec47962a07e0138aa0d8e6b0f0d60cb8e151d06303ce4ad0070f"},"q-08847e542ef9":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Yield of infectious viruses per cell","explanation":"Burst size is the number of infectious progeny virus particles released or produced per infected cell in one replication cycle.","optionReasons":{"C":"Burst size is the number of infectious progeny virus particles released or produced per infected cell in one replication cycle."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e655ce1f0f18fc65615ad90fe26cd107caf82cbcb41701c5c9583e4bf1f4f054"},"q-b0df20382700":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Are prone to mutation","explanation":"Many RNA viruses mutate relatively rapidly because their polymerases lack robust proofreading, although mutation rates vary and coronavirus polymerases have proofreading activity.","optionReasons":{"C":"Many RNA viruses mutate relatively rapidly because their polymerases lack robust proofreading, although mutation rates vary and coronavirus polymerases have proofreading activity."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0b9b4e85f691e02086ab09f20697804ced08e24e91556227713601a44c2c136d"},"q-a8c875af87cd":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Herpesviridae","explanation":"Herpesviridae are enveloped double-stranded DNA viruses, while papillomaviruses, polyomaviruses, adenoviruses and parvoviruses are nonenveloped.","optionReasons":{"A":"Herpesviridae are enveloped double-stranded DNA viruses, while papillomaviruses, polyomaviruses, adenoviruses and parvoviruses are nonenveloped."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"79d005cf2c40ef133ac37b9c9db485ddf3c03fb95cb7ef5b4286870ef3cdb621"},"q-e0a8023b3453":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Picornaviridae","explanation":"Picornaviruses are small nonenveloped positive-sense RNA viruses; the paramyxo-, toga-, flavi- and orthomyxovirus families are enveloped.","optionReasons":{"B":"Picornaviruses are small nonenveloped positive-sense RNA viruses; the paramyxo-, toga-, flavi- and orthomyxovirus families are enveloped."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9ae40a94a6aa2da8ed303316a8357b4af4ae97fc590d4d3b04634b77222c7873"},"q-7c1c9e320432":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Maintains sterile environments","explanation":"Normal microbiota contribute to colonization resistance, vitamin/metabolite production and immune maturation; they do not maintain all body environments sterile.","optionReasons":{"D":"Normal microbiota contribute to colonization resistance, vitamin/metabolite production and immune maturation; they do not maintain all body environments sterile."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"768c4a289697f130b44bfa8b6bc0eb3bc0fc17f3ece2c1a2f94c9bc7583deb9d"},"q-8d9d82047647":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Plasma gas","explanation":"Low-temperature plasma gas sterilization is used for certain instruments, not as an agent applied to intact skin for antisepsis.","optionReasons":{"D":"Low-temperature plasma gas sterilization is used for certain instruments, not as an agent applied to intact skin for antisepsis."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"12da16e763a554d203652f4df4629ac7a7006b9c11c3a8da69fa8731ef8a200d"},"q-9ced9f7b20fc":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Toxins","explanation":"Superantigens are secreted microbial toxins that cross-link MHC class II molecules and T-cell receptors outside conventional peptide-binding sites, causing excessive cytokine release.","optionReasons":{"E":"Superantigens are secreted microbial toxins that cross-link MHC class II molecules and T-cell receptors outside conventional peptide-binding sites, causing excessive cytokine release."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"246a9507d73a21f6113470d3ccc391a04a5a1208e3a46144e0cd8435b1f830ce"},"q-43c4f3bf11cb":{"correct":"B","answerText":"G- bacteria","explanation":"Lipopolysaccharide is an outer-membrane component of Gram-negative bacteria and can trigger strong inflammatory responses through lipid A recognition.","optionReasons":{"B":"Lipopolysaccharide is an outer-membrane component of Gram-negative bacteria and can trigger strong inflammatory responses through lipid A recognition."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4e8878a24877c7a84d36ab7726b1d87047e62c24d57d5ba1cf9f884a4fe86150"},"q-d76693198ed5":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Decrease in peripheral, presynaptic acetylcholine release, flaccid paralysis","explanation":"Botulinum neurotoxin cleaves SNARE proteins and prevents acetylcholine vesicle fusion at peripheral cholinergic terminals, causing flaccid paralysis.","optionReasons":{"E":"Botulinum neurotoxin cleaves SNARE proteins and prevents acetylcholine vesicle fusion at peripheral cholinergic terminals, causing flaccid paralysis."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b4cd789989c60f08530a8f27dd57a55f9771bdfe5de0f9e1a36bb1a648c05307"},"q-f36da9f0b511":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Activation of adenylate cyclase, increase in cAMP level, secretory diarrhea","explanation":"Cholera toxin ADP-ribosylates the Gs alpha subunit and maintains adenylate cyclase activity, increasing cAMP and causing profuse secretory watery diarrhea.","optionReasons":{"A":"Cholera toxin ADP-ribosylates the Gs alpha subunit and maintains adenylate cyclase activity, increasing cAMP and causing profuse secretory watery diarrhea."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"99d0aa03bc6898206e44fdf790112e7b396386228d6faab238ffb70d873fb957"},"q-de87ac9714af":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Decreased sugar transport","explanation":"Transformed cells often exhibit increased, not decreased, glucose transport and glycolysis as well as loss of contact inhibition and altered growth behavior.","optionReasons":{"C":"Transformed cells often exhibit increased, not decreased, glucose transport and glycolysis as well as loss of contact inhibition and altered growth behavior."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f060cbe098ddd52e89752f3110d6a9c73ed5bc7bc8a4beb4d27118c481ae2f73"},"q-cf8bc382aa20":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Mouth","explanation":"Stomatitis is inflammation of the oral mucosa, so the mouth is the relevant anatomical site.","optionReasons":{"C":"Stomatitis is inflammation of the oral mucosa, so the mouth is the relevant anatomical site."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6c5688823baf97cf29004f19ab524d30b9f07878063d1710c79416d148ada020"},"q-2adf43a34756":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Eyes","explanation":"Conjunctivitis involves inflammation of the conjunctival tissue lining the eyelids and anterior eyeball, so the eye is the affected site.","optionReasons":{"A":"Conjunctivitis involves inflammation of the conjunctival tissue lining the eyelids and anterior eyeball, so the eye is the affected site."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"54fdb8ce0f379bdfd45cd4404dc5eb2874cc1ea88ebe120277a92e4e1077f88d"},"q-4fc7c3bff75c":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Brain","explanation":"Meningitis affects the meninges surrounding the brain and spinal cord, making the CNS the relevant location among the listed sites.","optionReasons":{"B":"Meningitis affects the meninges surrounding the brain and spinal cord, making the CNS the relevant location among the listed sites."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"009a7e8297ecf4cf8842f57578a2c00a60395d6b2289d684187c51cf63d241d1"},"q-a320c4c95d26":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Enteric","explanation":"Rotavirus infects intestinal enterocytes and causes infantile gastroenteritis and diarrhea, making the enteric system the target.","optionReasons":{"B":"Rotavirus infects intestinal enterocytes and causes infantile gastroenteritis and diarrhea, making the enteric system the target."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"75823bf1c0bab3fc0eb388532bec2fda371d45f9fba4cc66e1e56d9061775552"},"q-db777772d167":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Binging Match the following descriptions with their terms:","explanation":"Fever, malaise, headache and myalgia are classic influenza-like symptoms; binge eating is not a standard clinical feature of viral infection.","optionReasons":{"E":"Fever, malaise, headache and myalgia are classic influenza-like symptoms; binge eating is not a standard clinical feature of viral infection."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"993b938e2db7d79d72539f30ea69abd776f1358e1dd941f3ebee8bba5e689d47"},"q-7e7785f19ad9":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Antibiotics","explanation":"Antibiotics are ineffective for routine prevention of transmission of viral infections because they target bacteria; hygiene, precautions and immunization are relevant preventive measures.","optionReasons":{"D":"Antibiotics are ineffective for routine prevention of transmission of viral infections because they target bacteria; hygiene, precautions and immunization are relevant preventive measures."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"371cd84ec7ebb31dea402f92a7f368be6df73369992abc2f9649ad64965f53c7"},"q-64339036b181":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Hand washing","explanation":"Hand hygiene is a cornerstone of infection prevention because it interrupts hand-mediated pathogen transmission between people and contaminated surfaces.","optionReasons":{"D":"Hand hygiene is a cornerstone of infection prevention because it interrupts hand-mediated pathogen transmission between people and contaminated surfaces."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"50eaa6a87250cebe2b914d20975e5342362e5991f880cab4cd40e2859a7e0e2e"},"q-895fb91db08f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"G+ cocci","explanation":"Staphylococci are Gram-positive spherical bacteria, typically appearing as grape-like clusters on a Gram-stained preparation.","optionReasons":{"D":"Staphylococci are Gram-positive spherical bacteria, typically appearing as grape-like clusters on a Gram-stained preparation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b7e1454db2b0223a13098772116519079751c6036ee6faa13309098bbdd05977"},"q-f314349f5394":{"correct":"A","answerText":"A ratio used to evaluate the safety and usefulness of a drug for indication","explanation":"The therapeutic index compares doses associated with toxic and therapeutic effects (classically TD50/ED50), serving as a rough measure of relative drug safety.","optionReasons":{"A":"The therapeutic index compares doses associated with toxic and therapeutic effects (classically TD50/ED50), serving as a rough measure of relative drug safety."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"da3181b1c23f0b67a0c632dbe2d87ae067534e05717428736c3593ebdb940d95"},"q-2caf53b3dc1b":{"correct":"B","answerText":"B and C fibers","explanation":"Small autonomic B fibers and many small-diameter C fibers are particularly susceptible to local anesthetic blockade; large myelinated motor A-alpha fibers generally require greater exposure.","optionReasons":{"B":"Small autonomic B fibers and many small-diameter C fibers are particularly susceptible to local anesthetic blockade; large myelinated motor A-alpha fibers generally require greater exposure."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c37a8b981dabcec56b9ae4a1b5d9133fd0cf671f80e0ec203c1579d536c122df"},"q-7f1fdf2117e9":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Mydriasis","explanation":"Organophosphate and other cholinesterase-inhibitor poisoning causes cholinergic miosis rather than mydriasis, alongside sweating, secretions, bronchospasm and gastrointestinal hypermotility.","optionReasons":{"B":"Organophosphate and other cholinesterase-inhibitor poisoning causes cholinergic miosis rather than mydriasis, alongside sweating, secretions, bronchospasm and gastrointestinal hypermotility."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bca3deffbd9d68a0474a2a7f343ff391bee39489e1f10db17a8764730dcdd747"},"q-58c9c49921d9":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Ephedrine","explanation":"Ephedrine is not a catecholamine because it lacks the catechol ring; epinephrine, norepinephrine and isoproterenol have catechol structures.","optionReasons":{"A":"Ephedrine is not a catecholamine because it lacks the catechol ring; epinephrine, norepinephrine and isoproterenol have catechol structures."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3b86ff8103309d083be3761858fc7afcc071f57d0abfefd293e97d5e12167b09"},"q-7c95ee66906f":{"correct":"B","answerText":"It increases heart rate, contractility and cardiac output","explanation":"Methoxamine primarily increases vascular resistance via alpha-1 activation, usually triggering reflex bradycardia rather than directly increasing cardiac rate and contractility.","optionReasons":{"B":"Methoxamine primarily increases vascular resistance via alpha-1 activation, usually triggering reflex bradycardia rather than directly increasing cardiac rate and contractility."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"afa53307af028d77a3f0804749089e9c7edefba3dcea862e691287c17f0e3908"},"q-7eb78d6a5b66":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Antagonism of presynaptic alfa2 receptors enhances norepinephrine release, which causes cardiac stimulation via unblocked beta receptors 31","explanation":"Blocking presynaptic alpha-2 autoreceptors increases norepinephrine release, which can stimulate unblocked cardiac beta-1 receptors and provoke tachycardia.","optionReasons":{"A":"Blocking presynaptic alpha-2 autoreceptors increases norepinephrine release, which can stimulate unblocked cardiac beta-1 receptors and provoke tachycardia."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3b1842a193c9c7ee13bb46df15a2f4ed84521ad86a1eff61288c04ecdeb668aa"},"q-1fd02192b0d5":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)","explanation":"Alpha-1 blockers such as tamsulosin and alfuzosin relax prostatic and bladder-neck smooth muscle to improve urinary outflow in benign prostatic hyperplasia.","optionReasons":{"C":"Alpha-1 blockers such as tamsulosin and alfuzosin relax prostatic and bladder-neck smooth muscle to improve urinary outflow in benign prostatic hyperplasia."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3f62c1f715a33f2e4cabd6058ff8a5e1598025a7751f0d7c1b3e0a8a909c32aa"},"q-3bc2c68e094a":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Metoprolol 33","explanation":"Metoprolol is relatively beta-1 selective and therefore has less bronchial beta-2 blockade than nonselective propranolol, nadolol or timolol, although caution is still required in asthma.","optionReasons":{"B":"Metoprolol is relatively beta-1 selective and therefore has less bronchial beta-2 blockade than nonselective propranolol, nadolol or timolol, although caution is still required in asthma."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8be47c4a2fa0bf2ac889f947f656fa4c8b667082989d3179382110ce62cf1bea"},"q-2767e661c72e":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phenobarbital","explanation":"Phenobarbital has a long elimination half-life and is more likely to accumulate and cause residual daytime sedation than short-acting hypnotics.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenobarbital has a long elimination half-life and is more likely to accumulate and cause residual daytime sedation than short-acting hypnotics."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e186504661ea98751ffbbeabfac46546b59ec7cbd04cb4e168616aabd7648bae"},"q-eb7b7698c1e8":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Zolpidem 36","explanation":"Zolpidem preferentially acts at the BZ1/omega-1 subtype of the GABA-A benzodiazepine receptor complex; flumazenil is an antagonist.","optionReasons":{"B":"Zolpidem preferentially acts at the BZ1/omega-1 subtype of the GABA-A benzodiazepine receptor complex; flumazenil is an antagonist."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dade98608b80156e35aff3b37870684cd4ba0305be00c61ce339a06f2f65b458"},"q-cc4eebd4d490":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Action on the medullar vasomotor center","explanation":"Severe sedative-hypnotic poisoning may depress medullary vasomotor regulation, producing hypotension and circulatory collapse.","optionReasons":{"C":"Severe sedative-hypnotic poisoning may depress medullary vasomotor regulation, producing hypotension and circulatory collapse."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6d21c077f308147e2a3e22e1a9cd765ac4d435ab74815fba967ab79d4807806a"},"q-b83fbb8d8c02":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Gingival hyperplasia","explanation":"Phenytoin can cause gingival overgrowth through changes in gingival connective-tissue turnover; other recognized toxicities include nystagmus and ataxia.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenytoin can cause gingival overgrowth through changes in gingival connective-tissue turnover; other recognized toxicities include nystagmus and ataxia."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"838be945de3010f535345c38e98f343dad418a7f439e88099d411736d1885145"},"q-d81c4bcd576b":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Lamotrigine","explanation":"Lamotrigine belongs to the phenyltriazine chemical class and reduces neuronal excitability principally via voltage-gated sodium-channel blockade.","optionReasons":{"C":"Lamotrigine belongs to the phenyltriazine chemical class and reduces neuronal excitability principally via voltage-gated sodium-channel blockade."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"41ecec7674fda5f68d24a2c140c47e20026b08caae66b0b9111fea4e47ca7268"},"q-e9b8fd99d3b3":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Zonisamide","explanation":"Zonisamide is a sulfonamide derivative that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and also inhibits T-type calcium currents.","optionReasons":{"B":"Zonisamide is a sulfonamide derivative that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and also inhibits T-type calcium currents."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"890b0e0c2b4cde70b84506fd1b9e54c81bee64ecf787e5e363a9a1eac268568b"},"q-8f350c525d97":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Chlorpromazine","explanation":"Chlorpromazine blocks dopamine D2 receptors and can cause drug-induced parkinsonism; benzodiazepines and carbamazepine do not have this typical dopamine-blocking effect.","optionReasons":{"A":"Chlorpromazine blocks dopamine D2 receptors and can cause drug-induced parkinsonism; benzodiazepines and carbamazepine do not have this typical dopamine-blocking effect."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d146b32300e39977bd24efec2feacf457da37617c4984522b6f41f25b5ecc2f8"},"q-718d41560230":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Clozapine","explanation":"Clozapine can reduce severe levodopa-associated psychosis with relatively little worsening of motor symptoms because of its unusual receptor-binding profile.","optionReasons":{"B":"Clozapine can reduce severe levodopa-associated psychosis with relatively little worsening of motor symptoms because of its unusual receptor-binding profile."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4bdbc4304d89cf87baaea3b5061e060df08dc5d0af892aebb691bf5d432c8e41"},"q-733b0d5fbc1c":{"correct":"B","answerText":"B and C fibers","explanation":"Small autonomic B fibers and many small-diameter C fibers are particularly susceptible to local anesthetic blockade; large myelinated motor A-alpha fibers generally require greater exposure.","optionReasons":{"B":"Small autonomic B fibers and many small-diameter C fibers are particularly susceptible to local anesthetic blockade; large myelinated motor A-alpha fibers generally require greater exposure."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c37a8b981dabcec56b9ae4a1b5d9133fd0cf671f80e0ec203c1579d536c122df"},"q-afc2d1577551":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Mydriasis","explanation":"Organophosphate and other cholinesterase-inhibitor poisoning causes cholinergic miosis rather than mydriasis, alongside sweating, secretions, bronchospasm and gastrointestinal hypermotility.","optionReasons":{"B":"Organophosphate and other cholinesterase-inhibitor poisoning causes cholinergic miosis rather than mydriasis, alongside sweating, secretions, bronchospasm and gastrointestinal hypermotility."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bca3deffbd9d68a0474a2a7f343ff391bee39489e1f10db17a8764730dcdd747"},"q-d5169a770715":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Ephedrine","explanation":"Ephedrine is not a catecholamine because it lacks the catechol ring; epinephrine, norepinephrine and isoproterenol have catechol structures.","optionReasons":{"A":"Ephedrine is not a catecholamine because it lacks the catechol ring; epinephrine, norepinephrine and isoproterenol have catechol structures."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3b86ff8103309d083be3761858fc7afcc071f57d0abfefd293e97d5e12167b09"},"q-506b68652e82":{"correct":"B","answerText":"It increases heart rate, contractility and cardiac output","explanation":"Methoxamine primarily increases vascular resistance via alpha-1 activation, usually triggering reflex bradycardia rather than directly increasing cardiac rate and contractility.","optionReasons":{"B":"Methoxamine primarily increases vascular resistance via alpha-1 activation, usually triggering reflex bradycardia rather than directly increasing cardiac rate and contractility."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"afa53307af028d77a3f0804749089e9c7edefba3dcea862e691287c17f0e3908"},"q-8e9c0618cca2":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Metoprolol 33","explanation":"Metoprolol is relatively beta-1 selective and therefore has less bronchial beta-2 blockade than nonselective propranolol, nadolol or timolol, although caution is still required in asthma.","optionReasons":{"B":"Metoprolol is relatively beta-1 selective and therefore has less bronchial beta-2 blockade than nonselective propranolol, nadolol or timolol, although caution is still required in asthma."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8be47c4a2fa0bf2ac889f947f656fa4c8b667082989d3179382110ce62cf1bea"},"q-ad3dd98aeab5":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phenobarbital","explanation":"Phenobarbital has a long elimination half-life and is more likely to accumulate and cause residual daytime sedation than short-acting hypnotics.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenobarbital has a long elimination half-life and is more likely to accumulate and cause residual daytime sedation than short-acting hypnotics."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e186504661ea98751ffbbeabfac46546b59ec7cbd04cb4e168616aabd7648bae"},"q-821a19b065e0":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Lamotrigine","explanation":"Lamotrigine belongs to the phenyltriazine chemical class and reduces neuronal excitability principally via voltage-gated sodium-channel blockade.","optionReasons":{"C":"Lamotrigine belongs to the phenyltriazine chemical class and reduces neuronal excitability principally via voltage-gated sodium-channel blockade."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"41ecec7674fda5f68d24a2c140c47e20026b08caae66b0b9111fea4e47ca7268"},"q-c07ba2e26d29":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Zonisamide","explanation":"Zonisamide is a sulfonamide derivative that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and also inhibits T-type calcium currents.","optionReasons":{"B":"Zonisamide is a sulfonamide derivative that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and also inhibits T-type calcium currents."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"890b0e0c2b4cde70b84506fd1b9e54c81bee64ecf787e5e363a9a1eac268568b"},"q-1e7b643a7623":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Clozapine","explanation":"Clozapine can reduce severe levodopa-associated psychosis with relatively little worsening of motor symptoms because of its unusual receptor-binding profile.","optionReasons":{"B":"Clozapine can reduce severe levodopa-associated psychosis with relatively little worsening of motor symptoms because of its unusual receptor-binding profile."},"references":[],"review":"exact_content_duplicate_of_new_reasoned_provisional","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4bdbc4304d89cf87baaea3b5061e060df08dc5d0af892aebb691bf5d432c8e41"},"q-569217b9d9cf":{"correct":"","answerText":"A butterfly-shaped endocrine gland in the anterior neck, with two lateral lobes joined by an isthmus anterior to the upper trachea.","explanation":"The thyroid lies roughly at C5–T1, inferior to the larynx. Follicular cells produce thyroid hormones, while parafollicular C cells secrete calcitonin.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"68581a122a029ffb1ca9c7cfd4950357593d5281b39a3816b3704f8ae0650cef","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-8ecbee985ac2":{"correct":"","answerText":"The subclavian vein lies posterior to the clavicle and anterior to the anterior scalene muscle, joining the internal jugular vein to form the brachiocephalic vein.","explanation":"Unlike the subclavian artery, which passes posterior to anterior scalene, the subclavian vein passes anterior to it. This relationship is important in central venous cannulation.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c20e063802157550805a23bc52717ad42d444c08d57ecfcbe98a3ed2ec446255","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-aef766e496e3":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hydroxyapatite crystals, predominantly calcium phosphate: Ca10(PO4)6(OH)2.","explanation":"Hydroxyapatite mineralizes the collagen-rich osteoid, providing compressive strength while collagen provides tensile resilience.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"66ff564417a76ebe82183adb0ad2748fd662a6735b2b2056f427be75601f214d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-86babeb9fb45":{"correct":"","answerText":"Woven (immature) bone.","explanation":"Woven bone has randomly oriented collagen and forms rapidly during fetal development and fracture repair. It is gradually replaced by more organized lamellar bone.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"60cefbdbd61c51dbe07e6abf12d4a6a70209466a133c2a5471f93f255b717693","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-d5a519226e59":{"correct":"","answerText":"The vagus nerve (CN X) is a mixed nerve carrying branchial motor, parasympathetic, visceral sensory, and some general somatic sensory fibers.","explanation":"It supplies motor fibers to most pharyngeal/laryngeal muscles and parasympathetic fibers to thoracic and much of the abdominal viscera; visceral afferents carry reflex information.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f6a33cdef8c3fced5553faa97bc0ca77e4de4b11566592a524610a67a60aa758","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-ddbb3dfd73c0":{"correct":"","answerText":"The vagus nerve (CN X) is mixed: parasympathetic visceral motor, branchial motor, visceral sensory, special sensory taste, and somatic sensory fibers.","explanation":"Its principal roles include autonomic regulation of heart, airways and gut as well as swallowing and phonation.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f6a33cdef8c3fced5553faa97bc0ca77e4de4b11566592a524610a67a60aa758","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-8d6272c998fd":{"correct":"","answerText":"Isolated thrombocytopenia with otherwise usually normal red-cell and white-cell lines.","explanation":"Immune thrombocytopenia produces antibody-mediated platelet destruction and impaired production; mucocutaneous bleeding and petechiae may occur.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9389c49fea155f9196d3622be7295043c7ee8ffd90eae948ec38902b14b3c729","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f4cfbb3f006b":{"correct":"","answerText":"Pancytopenia with a hypocellular, fatty bone marrow.","explanation":"Aplastic anemia is failure of hematopoietic stem-cell production. Low red cells, white cells and platelets cause fatigue, infections and bleeding.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b19e2958a945a20b1f19a75d0d476762e9a548987e7ee944bc712cbc158b0a8d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-506b7f781f10":{"correct":"","answerText":"Pancytopenia with a hypocellular, fatty bone marrow.","explanation":"Aplastic anemia impairs all three major marrow cell lines, producing anemia, neutropenia and thrombocytopenia.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b19e2958a945a20b1f19a75d0d476762e9a548987e7ee944bc712cbc158b0a8d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-85fc657ed2a5":{"correct":"","answerText":"Bone tissue is specialized vascularized connective tissue with cells embedded in mineralized extracellular matrix.","explanation":"Its matrix contains type I collagen and hydroxyapatite. Osteoblasts form bone, osteocytes maintain it and osteoclasts resorb it.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"00e4321e6a3c39118160fac1511dd7bf17340e23c423455a57d068400c7de11f","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-5762f03d8840":{"correct":"","answerText":"By shape: long, short, flat, irregular and sesamoid bones; by architecture: cortical (compact) and trabecular (spongy) bone.","explanation":"For example, femur is long, carpals short, sternum flat, vertebrae irregular and patella sesamoid. Compact and spongy describe internal structure.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"81ed5b28f3a848a5a3444574a7f7f1a78f2928e9474843b76da28c8b18c1aba8","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0ea8c28894b5":{"correct":"","answerText":"Support, movement, organ protection, mineral storage, hematopoiesis and fat storage.","explanation":"Bones provide levers for skeletal muscles, protect brain and thoracic organs, hold calcium/phosphate, and house red marrow for blood-cell formation.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"45c98e5497f49d3abb55e4563db876869afbec36149e61981c9907d2aafb50f0","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-12454bfaca54":{"correct":"","answerText":"The somatic nervous system conducts voluntary motor commands to skeletal muscle and carries conscious sensory signals from skin, joints and muscles.","explanation":"It comprises somatic motor neurons and somatic sensory afferents in peripheral nerves; somatic motor output usually uses a single neuron from CNS to muscle.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ba818afd1374870b79d3ba758df181311ee92a8c6e7f27baca7de4e5994e35f1","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-3f8b86fcca70":{"correct":"","answerText":"Right upper, left upper, right lower and left lower abdominal quadrants.","explanation":"Two perpendicular planes through the umbilicus divide the abdomen into four clinically useful regions for describing pain and examination findings.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"88386d96f1a7d07a102ec8073257ebe74a14b4473e5d1ce493a5e215aa0782f5","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e338cd380dc8":{"correct":"","answerText":"Carbon, hydrogen, oxygen and nitrogen.","explanation":"These four elements dominate proteins: amino acids contain carbon skeletons, amino and carboxyl groups; some also contain sulfur.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"48119f405348f755a3e4ef97145cab5a0355e6515b24d866abd90f6c33baf452","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-9f6d63e1d749":{"correct":"","answerText":"Epithelial tissue is a continuous sheet of tightly connected cells covering surfaces, lining cavities and forming glands.","explanation":"It has apical–basal polarity, rests on a basement membrane and is avascular; nutrients diffuse from underlying connective tissue.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"142cd81bea3b276370c61147133d7f731f8f3ab34a4a8a56ad5f6aba75c31639","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e20d294ef51d":{"correct":"","answerText":"Simple, stratified and pseudostratified epithelia, classified further as squamous, cuboidal or columnar; transitional epithelium is specialized for stretch.","explanation":"A single layer is simple, multiple layers stratified and pseudostratified appears layered but all cells touch the basement membrane.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a9957ffe299f43c3582eb0c3a0e62a2521fbb98d135fd978552cf75489a634ce","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-498cff1fa40e":{"correct":"","answerText":"Protection, absorption, secretion, diffusion, filtration, excretion and sensory reception.","explanation":"Keratinized stratified squamous epithelium protects skin, simple squamous facilitates gas exchange, and intestinal columnar epithelium absorbs nutrients.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b7bd26b74a9d544b51577db562acad9698eeee5a129f9238eec59c9d5385c0f8","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-4cca42457259":{"correct":"","answerText":"Connective tissue is mesenchyme-derived tissue whose cells are dispersed in an extracellular matrix of fibers and ground substance.","explanation":"Its major components include fibroblasts, collagen/elastin fibers and proteoglycan-rich ground substance; specialized forms include cartilage, bone and blood.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"31acb11cb569c5d210579093b795e2177681930790b5a095f36dcb9b157e8655","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-3f96ae67342e":{"correct":"","answerText":"Fibroblasts, adipocytes, macrophages, mast cells, plasma cells and migrating leukocytes; specialized connective tissues also contain chondrocytes and osteocytes.","explanation":"Fibroblasts synthesize matrix, macrophages phagocytose material and mast cells release inflammatory mediators.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"975408d83a8fd0f8dd9f40cef827e1eacec1a981090f3dba1d356a928ae21f2f","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-849f907fc2a0":{"correct":"","answerText":"Support, binding, protection, immune defense, nutrient storage, repair and transport.","explanation":"Collagen provides mechanical strength; adipose tissue stores energy; blood transports substances; immune cells participate in defense and healing.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5060752123eda7e93c9c6b25d9164131b97c37e60ba82fefccd30605d55ca723","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-76f68da8f192":{"correct":"","answerText":"Disorders affecting connective tissue, including autoimmune rheumatic diseases and inherited matrix disorders.","explanation":"Examples include systemic lupus erythematosus, systemic sclerosis, rheumatoid arthritis, Marfan syndrome and Ehlers–Danlos syndromes; their mechanisms differ.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5b77468b2bf16c81ce7f35f50825a90568b6ebd9cbb552d3997578d52f97b8af","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-1816a9805ca7":{"correct":"","answerText":"Examples include rheumatoid arthritis, systemic lupus erythematosus, systemic sclerosis, Sjögren syndrome and mixed connective tissue disease.","explanation":"These are autoimmune/connective-tissue disorders with distinct organ involvement; inherited connective tissue disorders such as Marfan syndrome form a separate category.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"07e1d5f20643456b16d78c4ba1acaddcf0fe7c53842349b6359e33fdf1b7a4bb","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e036d193b1c1":{"correct":"","answerText":"A bulla is a fluid-filled skin blister greater than approximately 5 mm in diameter (some classifications use 10 mm).","explanation":"It arises from separation within or below the epidermis and may result from burns, friction or autoimmune blistering disorders.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"49a78b25a26a4530f1fc667defc47e82360828843c2157c9a239690145f68340","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-d7764c08441f":{"correct":"","answerText":"Catagen phase.","explanation":"Catagen is the brief involution/regression phase of the hair cycle, between the growth (anagen) and resting (telogen) phases.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8e8aff0f4b1ea17c2c5ee064283853a63b0e1ae963c3aec5b59d0c87a0ae3a52","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-5c4c0335e44b":{"correct":"","answerText":"Cancer is a malignant neoplasm characterized by uncontrolled cell growth with capacity for local invasion and potentially metastasis.","explanation":"Genetic and epigenetic alterations confer growth advantage, resistance to death and other malignant capabilities; not every tumor is cancerous.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a94531574013a47781a056647295ffbc436486f8fba0e0af65bad96a03000545","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-c1d605d77541":{"correct":"","answerText":"Benign tumors generally remain localized, whereas malignant tumors invade surrounding tissues and may metastasize.","explanation":"Benign lesions are often well differentiated and slow growing; malignant lesions may display atypia, rapid growth, tissue destruction and vascular/lymphatic spread.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"74d8407f9c0b81f5f9ff9597f93ba3b7fc3a804b381a5458b27fab1766fac408","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-da327e723ea2":{"correct":"","answerText":"Cancer risks include tobacco, alcohol, infections, radiation, hereditary predisposition, age, obesity and some occupational/environmental exposures.","explanation":"Carcinogenesis results from accumulated genetic/epigenetic changes; modifiable exposures and inherited susceptibility interact.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"aeeae673d46e7a23b3d3889055fc86fd6517fc0699d271b320cd3f85aae36860","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-a8cbc395c5d1":{"correct":"","answerText":"Inflammation is the coordinated vascular and cellular response of living tissue to infection, injury or other harmful stimuli.","explanation":"It aims to eliminate the cause, clear damaged cells and initiate repair. Acute inflammation is typically neutrophil-rich; chronic inflammation is often macrophage/lymphocyte-rich.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bb5c8df127aef8d9d4c52aa5de3af08515837ccd78ba31ca53d67bf3d4005cec","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-67818f924f35":{"correct":"","answerText":"Infections, physical injury, chemical agents, ischemic tissue death, foreign bodies and immune reactions.","explanation":"Tissue damage or microbial products activate resident immune cells, initiating mediator release and recruitment of leukocytes.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"65dafb9691a7f0f07ed6286a60b8935a61f240b13ff63ed3557adfd3560e560e","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f31f3c954d9a":{"correct":"","answerText":"Redness (rubor), warmth (calor), swelling (tumor), pain (dolor), and loss of function (functio laesa).","explanation":"Vasodilation causes redness and warmth, increased vascular permeability causes edema, and inflammatory mediators stimulate nociceptors.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"21696616d25cd1258c003e6d59aa1ae0d88106e13fdd0a067a40fb39889ec3f4","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f4e768206fef":{"correct":"","answerText":"Cirrhosis is diffuse hepatic fibrosis with regenerative nodules that distort normal liver architecture.","explanation":"Chronic injury triggers stellate-cell activation and matrix deposition, causing portal hypertension, impaired synthetic function and risk of hepatocellular carcinoma.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5945523a5b28e8b4ac75e20190bc6c463cfd9f8fd01f7ca562854aa71db7de9d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0b0e122ac141":{"correct":"","answerText":"Acute abdomen refers to sudden or rapidly progressive severe abdominal symptoms requiring urgent assessment for potentially surgical pathology.","explanation":"Causes include perforation, obstruction, ischemia, appendicitis and intra-abdominal hemorrhage; not every acute abdomen requires surgery.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e02cb99c87d8bf9a8242f550e8ffd0e80b427c4e342424f4e0656e2bac6ece5f","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f58c8db7661c":{"correct":"","answerText":"History taking identifies the patient's problems, generates differential diagnoses, guides investigations and establishes clinical context and risk factors.","explanation":"Chronology, associated symptoms, medications, past history and patient priorities often narrow the diagnosis before examination or testing.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"053f53f6388abc25d1013c5c7d1aaa0292a05b7f33b8fcd602acb4bf3b5c0d07","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-61ebbe74dcc8":{"correct":"","answerText":"A diagnosis is the identification of a disease or clinical condition from history, examination and, where indicated, investigation.","explanation":"A working diagnosis can be revised as additional evidence arrives; a differential diagnosis lists plausible alternatives.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d122497f8c4246d3bd885a40b07b5f84b73130c5e5641d89e1db051629c10f66","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-25ced8cb7b88":{"correct":"","answerText":"Developmental milestones are age-linked functional abilities acquired during childhood across motor, language, cognitive and social domains.","explanation":"They help monitor development, recognizing that normal timing varies and delay requires context-specific assessment.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3b70b07f73ce86f31beda2c617426aac36356bf0e1095e5616b7a05ae6cac4ea","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-476eec1aee41":{"correct":"","answerText":"Periumbilical pain migrating to the right iliac fossa, anorexia, nausea or vomiting and sometimes fever.","explanation":"Visceral midgut pain is initially central; parietal peritoneal involvement localizes pain to the right lower abdomen. Presentations vary, especially in children, pregnancy and older adults.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a84436756f72f64c14d36ef0460edf2aafd4eff3436ec2caf195c71ed1dba883","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-bbb8c6cadfd6":{"correct":"","answerText":"Right lower quadrant tenderness, guarding, rebound/percussion tenderness and sometimes fever; Rovsing, psoas and obturator signs may occur.","explanation":"Focal peritoneal irritation produces localized pain and guarding, but no single sign rules appendicitis in or out.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"065f20d0a162cb5ad81a6cccdfcc70ae8be85a05d3479562da62d5d01df8d4b8","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-bcf5bf43c7cb":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hemorrhoids, anal fissure, perianal abscess, anal fistula and rectal prolapse.","explanation":"These common anorectal conditions differ in presentation: bleeding/itching, painful defecation, suppuration, draining tract and protrusion respectively.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d26e382f41c0d86945b82407f5b18cef21360077c2b8bdd956c501fed6c4dcf5","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-218f81243f21":{"correct":"","answerText":"Cataracts are opacities of the crystalline lens that reduce light transmission and degrade vision.","explanation":"Age-related lens protein changes cause gradual painless blurring and glare; clinically significant cataract is treated by lens extraction and intraocular lens implantation.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"17119592327dd54ee416817fcb7c93551d37dd40486847f89290be86d60d8bf0","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-16bff458f810":{"correct":"","answerText":"The eye is the organ of vision that focuses light on photoreceptors in the retina and sends neural signals along the optic pathway.","explanation":"Cornea and lens refract light, retinal rods/cones transduce photons, and the optic nerve transmits signals to visual centers.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3ed075b16f1f929ef8144f06d447fe52cbd4a2068934f59bc9336126d0300ffc","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-cfbd342a7b22":{"correct":"","answerText":"Cornea, sclera, conjunctiva, iris, ciliary body, lens, choroid, retina, aqueous/vitreous chambers and optic nerve.","explanation":"These structures together focus light, regulate its entry, maintain ocular shape and transform it into neural signals.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"58bb6956da96b1b135c31370977b4628b1df583860c5d3a476a8eb05bf12b2b4","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-28968c21078a":{"correct":"","answerText":"Cornea/lens focus light; iris controls pupil size; retina detects light; ciliary body produces aqueous humor and accommodates; sclera protects; optic nerve conducts signals.","explanation":"Aqueous humor supports intraocular pressure and corneal/lens nutrition, whereas the choroid supplies the outer retina.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"854280b7c081b348b0023da1d2a1188f736f7d206cf74d30174bf237e2c3f09c","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-4999619cc88b":{"correct":"","answerText":"Refractive errors, cataract, glaucoma, conjunctivitis, keratitis, uveitis, retinal disease and age-related macular degeneration.","explanation":"Different tissues cause characteristic symptoms such as blur, pain/redness, field loss or central vision impairment.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"43ffeb4bf7df6d65d08faf60d2f9cb66a5b05f92f19abe0273de0c4d74f2feee","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-500e4a672d83":{"correct":"","answerText":"Protein-energy malnutrition is inadequate energy and/or protein intake or utilization causing impaired growth and body composition.","explanation":"Severe acute malnutrition may present as wasting (marasmus), nutritional edema (kwashiorkor), or both, and increases infectious morbidity.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b2cdb9fdff529f452a24fa56c1d1e76f374f01fc90e63b26d058e797e3943279","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-a9a5841f1529":{"correct":"","answerText":"Growth failure, immune dysfunction, recurrent infections, anemia, micronutrient deficiency, hypothermia and, in severe cases, organ dysfunction.","explanation":"Insufficient nutrients impair immune defenses, tissue repair and metabolism, creating a cycle of illness and worsening malnutrition.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9d1c1303e6143e11a36c11491b332a5f69c68496bbe6219457ffff83b39074bc","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-08faf706fd83":{"correct":"","answerText":"Kwashiorkor may cause nutritional edema, fatty liver, skin/hair changes and infection; marasmus causes severe wasting, weakness and impaired thermoregulation.","explanation":"The syndromes can overlap; both increase risk of hypoglycemia, hypothermia, dehydration and infection.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"882f7f618cad8f6b7d0a42d5618cec2f0cad7b16a1c424f36e975c44bb48bf0a","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-29bd1b9b767a":{"correct":"","answerText":"Obesity is abnormal or excessive adiposity that impairs health; in adults it is commonly screened using BMI of at least 30 kg/m².","explanation":"BMI is a practical surrogate and must be interpreted alongside body composition and metabolic risk, which vary by population.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8b59933e08908d5ca1d5afdb4d6f0b79e08ec8cdbbc76515cc856814cfdacecf","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-719cfed43279":{"correct":"","answerText":"Major causes include sustained positive energy balance influenced by diet, inactivity, sleep, genetics, medications and social/environmental factors.","explanation":"Rare endocrine or genetic disorders can contribute, but obesity is usually multifactorial rather than a single behavioral choice.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"75ac68653645e727cf547311b0f26e323e6e3dbf512c7dbacc7894897ff26425","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-600620072b2f":{"correct":"","answerText":"Type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease, hypertension, obstructive sleep apnea, fatty liver disease, osteoarthritis and some cancers.","explanation":"Excess adipose tissue promotes insulin resistance, inflammation and mechanical stress, producing metabolic and musculoskeletal complications.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8490caa896e42e499e62d7a31eede70546be5f4e253e26b6aea4c14920b4b6c7","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-78233bf5c79a":{"correct":"","answerText":"Chronic energy imbalance with genetic susceptibility, calorie-dense diets, low activity, sleep disturbances, medications and environmental determinants.","explanation":"Biology and environment influence hunger, satiety and energy expenditure, so obesity is not explained solely by willpower.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"71ee9b1297fea85596433ac5223075b3a53da479369087702588d95b458aad0d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-8eeac11b9a4e":{"correct":"","answerText":"Classify malnutrition by phenotype and context: undernutrition (wasting, stunting, underweight), micronutrient deficiencies, and overweight/obesity.","explanation":"In children, WHO anthropometric Z-scores and clinical edema help identify acute/chronic undernutrition; adults use BMI, weight loss and clinical assessment.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"78c85863306edeef8ef8039abbed1a4ae1a97c0db134149cac7f8d72116f3498","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-93835dde32ca":{"correct":"","answerText":"Examples include recurrent infections and impaired physical or cognitive growth.","explanation":"Protein-energy deficiency weakens immune function and limits nutrients required for tissue growth and repair.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a8dbe0a74244d443d40ca013dd40866e5d828d6aa298ba359f1a86fe4a682fd1","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-1ce3e7499be1":{"correct":"","answerText":"Vitamin K supports gamma-carboxylation of coagulation factors II, VII, IX, X and proteins C and S.","explanation":"Gamma-carboxylation permits calcium binding, allowing vitamin K-dependent coagulation proteins to function at phospholipid surfaces.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3cabf93be1746574adc875f43e682046c54a6f62415c28a269111263814b8765","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-69c82250e366":{"correct":"","answerText":"Vitamin K deficiency causes a bleeding tendency, often with prolonged prothrombin time/INR.","explanation":"Reduced functional vitamin K-dependent clotting factors impair hemostasis; newborns are particularly vulnerable without prophylaxis.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"eb571634b3ae79de1b20d413fcc3bc7b2b812700533284662dc19143cd342c2b","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-40412f1732f6":{"correct":"","answerText":"During proline and lysine hydroxylation of nascent collagen chains in the endoplasmic reticulum.","explanation":"Prolyl and lysyl hydroxylases require molecular oxygen, iron, alpha-ketoglutarate and vitamin C to maintain ferrous iron, stabilizing collagen triple helices.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4e61c2112fda2168b59ac36bb44dd1af347adb0a71afa10d6f13527364092318","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f699ba5b495c":{"correct":"","answerText":"A standard drink contains a defined mass of pure ethanol; the exact amount depends on national convention (e.g., 14 g in the United States).","explanation":"Drink volume alone is not a standard drink: the ethanol content depends on beverage strength and the definition used by the local authority.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ebc951c75682eba345dd72c8f39b5f7687f8bc9635e935f272fb5547c3174a76","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-b4d0eb3d92c7":{"correct":"","answerText":"Persistent cough, fever, night sweats, weight loss, fatigue and sometimes hemoptysis, depending on disease site.","explanation":"Pulmonary TB commonly causes subacute respiratory and systemic symptoms; extrapulmonary disease presents according to the affected organ.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"991a793e69904eade3f1ceaf2c37c711ee57fbe82e89968277a97b6968875251","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e55cdba895d7":{"correct":"","answerText":"20,004.2.","explanation":"The mean is the sum 2+3+7+9+100000 = 100021 divided by five. A single extreme value strongly shifts the mean upward.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ba6b5443f0681a2675bcb77a6a60df489e70ae683b8efe649ffa0cddde4658ed","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-1ae5456bf9a1":{"correct":"","answerText":"20,004.2.","explanation":"The arithmetic mean is 100021/5. The large outlier illustrates the mean's sensitivity to extreme values.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fe2112f087292436ef52468939768f2dd38d7f741d4465c5d6e4e97bba9ee586","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-3db332e33eb2":{"correct":"","answerText":"Random error is variability of estimates due to chance sampling or measurement fluctuations; it can be reduced through larger, well-designed samples and more precise measurement.","explanation":"Unlike systematic bias, random error does not predictably shift the estimate in one direction and is summarized with standard errors and confidence intervals.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"96354c9a5673ba1a22eac796a5b17407817eb73c73565af2a3cdf300f9749e90","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-6c89c4aea1c3":{"correct":"","answerText":"Selection bias, information/measurement bias, and confounding are major threats to epidemiologic validity.","explanation":"Reduce them through sound sampling, standardized/blinded measurements, restriction/matching/randomization where appropriate, and multivariable adjustment; sample size alone does not correct bias.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"63230cca84ad931f90bd535655cb4ae4f6eaa6bc3fac708f3e2c45ae20a98ae5","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-9044e7fa573d":{"correct":"","answerText":"Incidence proportion (risk), incidence rate, and prevalence are common disease-frequency measures.","explanation":"Incidence proportion counts new cases among those initially at risk over a period; incidence rate uses person-time; prevalence measures all existing cases at a specified time or interval.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"aacc267fcb76641de1d8d8e27eb844c6504949319b169c113a6c39ef44f75051","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-1cfc189af305":{"correct":"","answerText":"Breast cancer screening is testing asymptomatic people for early breast cancer, most commonly with mammography in eligible age/risk groups.","explanation":"The aim is to detect clinically meaningful cancers before symptoms, weighing mortality benefit against false positives and overdiagnosis; schedules vary by guideline.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4b4cc3e03267d926073628fd84c8ae0e3c44a55d40ab110fe25490b3b36d752f","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-73072c9b8779":{"correct":"","answerText":"Positive predictive value = true positives / (true positives + false positives).","explanation":"PPV is the probability of disease given a positive test; it depends on disease prevalence as well as test sensitivity and specificity.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4fb01171f5ec066dcfda9e51c6c15afe7a513b793590caeb24d537558c98e280","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-dd55eede3f18":{"correct":"","answerText":"Statistical inference draws conclusions about a population from sample data while accounting for uncertainty.","explanation":"Confidence intervals and hypothesis tests quantify sampling uncertainty under stated assumptions; they do not remove confounding or measurement bias.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4e82e9862c9fcc6798502442a38093afd231abf16758658b8587d4124eb734ee","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-c12893b10fd0":{"correct":"","answerText":"Title, abstract, introduction, methods, results, discussion, conclusion, references and, when applicable, acknowledgments/supplements.","explanation":"The IMRaD core (Introduction, Methods, Results, Discussion) supports transparent reporting and interpretation of research.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"82cd482c3ed395f5030ea85484d46254a37caa564bb8b615a3f877704132be7e","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-ad4bc92378e4":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hemostasis is the coordinated process of stopping bleeding after vessel injury while maintaining blood fluidity elsewhere.","explanation":"Vasoconstriction, platelet adhesion/aggregation, coagulation-mediated fibrin formation and later fibrinolysis work in sequence.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ff5614f0320cf5bd8c6dafe865aff6b3b14481d3eeff6372930dbc14e5724ed2","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-ebed420cbf14":{"correct":"","answerText":"Water (H2O).","explanation":"Formation of a peptide bond is a condensation reaction between amino and carboxyl groups, releasing one water molecule per new bond.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8248465af1b4648c849d2ed4574fe44a27977909792fa0512902e8396be0f200","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-baf7fd81a551":{"correct":"","answerText":"Both are glucose polymers, but cellulose has beta(1→4) linkages whereas amylose has alpha(1→4) linkages.","explanation":"Humans have amylases for alpha-linked starch but cannot hydrolyze cellulose beta(1→4) bonds, so cellulose functions as dietary fiber.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c24a78d89e169b46f23191ab2595712c939b19ab958d7e9949f9f4db9d357fd1","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f36aec170037":{"correct":"","answerText":"They are C4 epimers: alpha-D-glucose and alpha-D-galactose differ in configuration at carbon 4.","explanation":"Their alpha designation refers to configuration at the anomeric carbon (C1), not the C4 epimeric difference.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c1d010475128032ea0f2f47532d3015bcdf424e26f7ba2508da2f187709d193a","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-418a72cb8b86":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hypothyroidism commonly raises LDL cholesterol because thyroid hormone deficiency reduces hepatic LDL receptor activity and lipoprotein clearance.","explanation":"Triglycerides may also rise; correcting hypothyroidism often improves the lipid profile, although coexisting dyslipidemia may remain.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"aacedf172794cf4d03ef444ee683d32b6481294cfd56dc2e00e8dc7c85b74854","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-c340717fffea":{"correct":"","answerText":"Five coenzymes.","explanation":"The pyruvate dehydrogenase complex requires thiamine pyrophosphate, lipoamide, CoA, FAD and NAD+ for oxidative decarboxylation of pyruvate.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"adbf113b6c38e96e5a8a8fc96ee8af367ae8d40afc12c94f20ef7efebadf155f","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-c845d0329b59":{"correct":"","answerText":"Reversible addition or removal of a chemical group on an enzyme—commonly phosphorylation—to change enzyme function.","explanation":"Protein kinases add phosphate groups and phosphatases remove them; modification can increase or decrease catalytic activity depending on the target.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3d926da128281a4411e97b84f43370dee52f502fffa89cca9081fe7d1dfe1b0c","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-08d0e0f683c1":{"correct":"","answerText":"Four ATP are produced gross per glucose during glycolysis, but only two ATP are gained net.","explanation":"Glycolysis consumes two ATP in its preparatory phase and generates four through substrate-level phosphorylation.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"725ff84f287fb3ca3400bde2b9c62bbdab37ac402dd3f1b362d07d19f983ccd0","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-86874d520802":{"correct":"","answerText":"Glycine.","explanation":"Its side chain is one hydrogen atom, making it the smallest amino acid and the only standard amino acid without a chiral alpha carbon.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"98f6d24d2ad605ad5d2cc56fa2a7c4d0537f912d9ebc95e6003289160cb313f5","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-655074b704a7":{"correct":"","answerText":"Nucleotides, each made of a nitrogenous base, pentose sugar and phosphate group.","explanation":"Polymerization links nucleotides through phosphodiester bonds to form DNA or RNA strands.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"55aa753e6f26600a103f1bd489dc47b192ae5df0046c784d76aa99aca22996a7","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-c47c8d7c4ca9":{"correct":"","answerText":"A prosthetic group.","explanation":"A prosthetic group is a cofactor bound tightly, sometimes covalently, to an enzyme rather than associating loosely as a cosubstrate.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8d849bddaf399f0b860efab787d0d59553036b2454f63306bbe8b50eccdd5546","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-73278f6b87b3":{"correct":"","answerText":"Reverse transcriptase is a major retroviral antiviral target; integrase and protease are also drug targets.","explanation":"Retroviruses use reverse transcriptase to convert RNA into DNA, integrase to insert viral DNA into host DNA and protease to mature virions.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"18e6380a606f4b209e901824b8a3da1a73a4577fc8a9c77a369025e4e1aae44a","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-69ed6b1699b8":{"correct":"","answerText":"Competitive inhibitors occupy the active site and may be overcome by sufficient substrate; allosteric inhibitors bind elsewhere and alter catalytic activity/conformation.","explanation":"Under simple Michaelis–Menten assumptions, competitive inhibition increases apparent Km without changing Vmax; allosteric effects depend on the enzyme and regulator.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3492a90d56c3c5cfc0927120dc7e14e18aa91efe8ab637b51e2140eefd6d7d1b","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-392a699cb699":{"correct":"","answerText":"Ligand-gated ion channels, G protein-coupled receptors, receptor tyrosine kinases, cytokine/JAK–STAT receptors and intracellular/nuclear receptors are major signaling classes.","explanation":"Different receptor families transmit extracellular ligand binding into ion fluxes, second-messenger cascades, phosphorylation or altered transcription; intracellular receptors sense membrane-permeable ligands.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4ca24ed21c30d25ef8bd2919af7fb0522d1ad9043205793ca4acf99fe178d100","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-763409c085b6":{"correct":"","answerText":"Glucocorticoid receptor, estrogen receptor and thyroid-hormone receptor.","explanation":"These receptors are intracellular/nuclear and change gene transcription after binding lipophilic hormones, though localization and trafficking vary.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"40d54c22a0ed49029df71e0a2d914e61e85ff7a0fb389cb423e199d795b0447c","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-24af37defb94":{"correct":"","answerText":"Active tuberculosis is treated with a multidrug regimen selected for disease site, susceptibility, patient factors and local guidelines, often an initial isoniazid/rifampicin/pyrazinamide/ethambutol phase followed by isoniazid/rifampicin.","explanation":"Combination therapy prevents selection of resistant bacilli. Duration and drugs vary for resistance, meningeal disease and special populations.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"eda79c958c4dc3f28047cde1fa2b8bc7a11b22749730f0ba78077017e331e048","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-3c295e86d3b5":{"correct":"","answerText":"Type I (immediate) hypersensitivity, usually involving IgE-mediated mast-cell activation.","explanation":"Allergen cross-linking of surface IgE triggers histamine release and wheal-and-flare skin responses, though not every case of urticaria is IgE-mediated.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c7431bd8184a6008a4a3e5689ce9869dd6eb620b3c68db66aabdf3edec8f9146","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0dcbf722a085":{"correct":"","answerText":"Type I immediate hypersensitivity.","explanation":"Food-related urticaria appearing rapidly after exposure can involve allergen cross-linking IgE on mast cells, causing histamine release.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"79e3aeef90cc6bf56475b43fb15250885eda189755c87b6e2a12c919064906ba","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-6866d38797f4":{"correct":"","answerText":"Peptide antigens bound to MHC class II molecules on antigen-presenting cells.","explanation":"CD4 is a coreceptor for MHC class II; conventional CD4 helper T cells recognize presented peptide–MHC II complexes rather than free soluble antigen.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"997576fb510fc41af5ba5fcf93e9310a35b22eaad316401160565ebf953b0773","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-2426e9a40694":{"correct":"","answerText":"Mast cells (and basophils).","explanation":"Mast-cell granules contain heparin and histamine; these cells participate in allergic and inflammatory reactions.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6dbf77c3e52fe167974e75ba2217194ef60578a02f928b60f288d0764e34581b","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-84dbc3075130":{"correct":"","answerText":"Toxocara canis infects dogs mainly by ingesting embryonated eggs, transplacental transmission of larvae to puppies, and ingestion of infected paratenic hosts; humans acquire infection by ingesting eggs from contaminated soil or food.","explanation":"Larvae migrate through tissues and can cause visceral or ocular larva migrans in accidental human hosts.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c218ec816e9eeed4eb6cd75ba6cb6481f46b257bacfa51941db9767d577c1121","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-6d73698e94bc":{"correct":"","answerText":"A definitive host supports sexual reproduction or the adult sexually mature stage of a parasite; an intermediate host supports larval or asexual development.","explanation":"For malaria, the female Anopheles mosquito is the definitive host because Plasmodium undergoes sexual reproduction there, while humans are intermediate hosts.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b1715628aadb69762ac034c844227c1cc89bf410f421bd8ac91160e248c24026","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-826686a978c9":{"correct":"","answerText":"Schistosomiasis is acquired when free-swimming cercariae from infected freshwater snails penetrate human skin during contact with contaminated water.","explanation":"Humans shed eggs in urine or feces, miracidia infect snails, and snails release cercariae. Safe water, sanitation, snail control and praziquantel reduce transmission.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4ac696a32275f19c67a53a7b20cd814919c56e93870f0a1ad382b5aa07edf94a","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-eb5dd9539c67":{"correct":"","answerText":"Infected humans contaminate freshwater with schistosome eggs; miracidia infect compatible snails; the snails release cercariae that penetrate skin in contaminated water.","explanation":"Schistosomiasis is acquired through skin contact, not by swallowing cercariae; prevention targets water contact, sanitation and infected hosts.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"02f6f1a2c723a403766b0716ef6b4dabe0648eef6565afde8d77ef725f7cce4a","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-2492a7598220":{"correct":"","answerText":"Giardia attaches to small-intestinal mucosa using a ventral adhesive disc.","explanation":"Its trophozoites adhere mechanically without invading deeply, impairing absorption and producing greasy diarrhea or bloating.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f0b436b3ed69e19b6cf2aa4a51efc5fe222c3c23f1e7f9ce42d39a14deff00dd","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-1d1cdb6fbd8c":{"correct":"","answerText":"Filariasis is infection by filarial nematodes; elephantiasis is severe chronic enlargement and thickening of a limb or other tissue due to lymphatic damage.","explanation":"Lymphatic filariasis may lead to elephantiasis, but many infected people never develop it, and other conditions can cause limb swelling.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"282e61408b8e82dc512d122520a995b7e53a1650eecb034b84c100f346585028","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e0d267f6550e":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hookworm infection usually occurs when infective filariform larvae in contaminated soil penetrate bare skin, often the feet.","explanation":"Larvae migrate through blood and lungs, are swallowed and mature in the small intestine, where they may cause chronic iron-loss anemia.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"419dc923e5a84549809d968501848e3f8703fa1c53586bb37a6d43d040479796","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-d0726df5b5b7":{"correct":"","answerText":"Diphyllobothrium latum (traditionally the broad fish tapeworm; now often classified as Dibothriocephalus latus).","explanation":"Humans acquire infection by eating raw or insufficiently cooked infected freshwater fish containing plerocercoid larvae.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7ebb9888953ceb083ba99b54a684a732ae7fc8610e2783bcb92e8ac6ff8080cc","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-417e258dc292":{"correct":"","answerText":"New World hookworm.","explanation":"Necator americanus is a major human hookworm responsible for chronic intestinal blood loss and iron deficiency.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a289fb9530e5bb89dc8f65f521d25894119658487f5d9288117e6c2ed87fca1c","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-cf000ea3f451":{"correct":"","answerText":"Female Anopheles mosquitoes transmit sporozoites to humans; parasites multiply in hepatocytes, then erythrocytes, producing merozoites and gametocytes that mosquitoes ingest.","explanation":"Sexual reproduction and sporogony occur in mosquito midgut, producing salivary-gland sporozoites for the next bite.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"99e9a368c0c77e3beca4ef03d367df77714547f1b60a31b9b2c2e3d66b326b61","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-4976be3cd0c6":{"correct":"","answerText":"Schistosoma haematobium (urinary disease/hematuria), S. mansoni (intestinal and hepatosplenic disease), and S. japonicum (intestinal and hepatosplenic disease).","explanation":"Egg-induced granulomatous inflammation, rather than adult worm feeding alone, causes much tissue pathology.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b15f40708378742f6cc8bbaa6161c69a7be095119ed0a5d5513239bf0dbb4be8","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-00226e5ba32c":{"correct":"","answerText":"Nucleoside/nucleotide reverse transcriptase inhibitors and non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs and NNRTIs).","explanation":"Both inhibit HIV reverse transcriptase through different mechanisms; modern antiretroviral therapy also includes integrase and protease inhibitors.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4fcfba8d2f4704b0f281e547aea9fc87b2514a68a6621e3b5374aec3cb5eacf0","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-a1726f976dfb":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hepatitis A, B and C viruses (other examples include D and E).","explanation":"These are distinct viruses causing hepatic inflammation and differ in transmission and chronic-infection potential.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"12e8b134f6b0eecc62c227029a63e214994c62f1afadf04d50c7f97a3b846dea","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-fc3ddc606305":{"correct":"","answerText":"Sylvatic (jungle) and urban yellow-fever transmission cycles.","explanation":"Sylvatic transmission occurs between mosquitoes and nonhuman primates, with incidental human infection; urban transmission occurs between humans via Aedes mosquitoes.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dd4321f2fe7b5e5f1d4438bfd9a8229de810087d55816ab5783d810bedb32cb2","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-349bc3a9c945":{"correct":"","answerText":"Ebola virus and Marburg virus (examples of viral hemorrhagic fever agents).","explanation":"Both are filoviruses capable of causing severe systemic illness with vascular dysfunction; not every case has overt bleeding.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4ed9362dd983d7afe3194fbf2176ea4b3f42375f05d1567dbe4682ca619c3f88","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0d955980c8e8":{"correct":"","answerText":"Obtain multiple sets of blood cultures before antibiotics, where clinically feasible.","explanation":"Blood cultures identify sustained bacteremia and guide susceptibility-directed treatment; echocardiography is also central for diagnosing infective endocarditis.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"73127a707d662720a8dcc7ee0162a964b9899b83f6d8ecd3afcd954512f1d167","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-3f924d90707a":{"correct":"","answerText":"Insulin resistance combined with progressive pancreatic beta-cell dysfunction.","explanation":"Muscle/liver/adipose resistance increases insulin requirement; declining beta-cell reserve eventually causes persistent hyperglycemia.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"10c130551e0be1b7bfe8c038bc4375cdb50e312289345e029ff9658a47483fb6","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-005cd8d3c2bd":{"correct":"","answerText":"Insulin resistance with progressive loss of beta-cell compensatory secretion.","explanation":"Hepatic glucose output and impaired uptake contribute to type 2 diabetes; not all patients have obesity.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3ed44368a3a9866a922def96f22395a7abf444750580f900eaa68c81f1bea990","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-9a6105f91079":{"correct":"","answerText":"Exertional dyspnea, orthopnea, paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea, fatigue and peripheral edema are common heart-failure symptoms.","explanation":"Pulmonary congestion causes breathlessness while low forward output and fluid retention contribute to fatigue and swelling.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9a0862884f988f5aca796c5ae7efcab1b35bce89ba2b8dace99b211a1455e3d5","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-d59ec67a5573":{"correct":"","answerText":"Jaundice, ascites, variceal bleeding, splenomegaly, edema, encephalopathy and synthetic dysfunction are typical advanced-cirrhosis features.","explanation":"Portal hypertension and reduced liver synthetic/metabolic capacity explain most decompensation findings.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6733fa8b70c61df601c2803373d59aa253f27fb8f5e31312054fbaedc9dd54a3","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0295596c5ce4":{"correct":"","answerText":"Age, family history, excess sodium intake, obesity, inactivity, heavy alcohol intake, kidney disease, diabetes and obstructive sleep apnea.","explanation":"Hypertension is multifactorial; identifying reversible contributors improves prevention and management.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a321fc41d60023294455f906704805750fc94c012de3c07455ea4037c4104e08","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-5e95aa71d5ad":{"correct":"","answerText":"LABAs provide prolonged bronchodilation as add-on controller treatment, but in asthma they must be used with an inhaled corticosteroid rather than as LABA monotherapy.","explanation":"LABA alone does not treat airway inflammation and increases risk of severe asthma outcomes; ICS–formoterol combinations may also function as relievers depending on regimen.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"cbda6a0f7b7f8b2b999a7f333524d6648a5fffb6fd0c574b9521158cf97e5cc9","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-fdc4e3c9a8f5":{"correct":"","answerText":"At least 15 hours per day is the usual minimum for survival benefit from long-term oxygen therapy in qualifying severe chronic resting hypoxemia.","explanation":"Prescription requires confirmation of chronic hypoxemia and titration to saturation targets; not every patient with severe COPD needs oxygen.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"11788c24bd5da361a6fd56f78e5c003bb3894a8d261eb59f1f3864c8e28d207f","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-1e48be52f2c0":{"correct":"","answerText":"Polyuria, polydipsia, weight loss, fatigue, blurred vision, recurrent infections and poor wound healing.","explanation":"Excess glucose produces osmotic diuresis and dehydration; severe insulin deficiency may progress to ketosis or hyperosmolar crisis.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ce2cceb330a941be7c527d184d68ca964a99c01acdcbccb3cd0a5293f5dafb47","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-033da39669e4":{"correct":"","answerText":"BCG is generally contraindicated in significant immunodeficiency, including symptomatic HIV infection, and in pregnancy; defer vaccination in acutely ill infants according to local guidance.","explanation":"BCG is a live attenuated Mycobacterium bovis vaccine that can disseminate in severely immunocompromised recipients. HIV policies vary by patient context and national guideline.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a21acbf1e64581e46476f75d912ba2504ac59fe854e2bba02e32909834597c95","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-4176a13f8069":{"correct":"","answerText":"Fetal circulation uses placental gas exchange and three shunts: ductus venosus, foramen ovale and ductus arteriosus.","explanation":"Oxygenated placental blood enters via the umbilical vein; shunts bypass much of fetal liver and lungs, which are not yet used for oxygenation.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a6f06b430eda123d912f863ef4f22ebb3711dee832a72db266b6811b1827db03","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-97f8379d56ef":{"correct":"","answerText":"Lethargy/unconsciousness, sunken eyes, inability or poor ability to drink, and very slow skin-pinch recoil.","explanation":"These are WHO-style assessment signs of severe dehydration in children with diarrhea; two or more qualifying signs support classification.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"213129e818e7515192083be8bfd8681bf6a41208a6a6133901afa1f1ae886c11","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-b61111b1aeb9":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hypotonia, characteristic facial features (upslanting palpebral fissures, epicanthic folds), a single transverse palmar crease and developmental delay.","explanation":"Down syndrome results most often from trisomy 21; congenital heart disease and gastrointestinal anomalies may accompany it.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fddad46496c69925a765041b8dd4164a36be3d3ec38023474e385ae2a0615590","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e52872900091":{"correct":"","answerText":"Poor feeding, temperature instability, lethargy/irritability, seizures or bulging fontanelle.","explanation":"Neonatal meningitis may lack classic neck stiffness; subtle sepsis-like features should prompt urgent assessment.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7614c9aedc85a64b36cf878ae76af5712ae8ebbcb95aac6830b6de2c8b046377","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0c93ffb566be":{"correct":"","answerText":"Sensorineural hearing loss, epilepsy, developmental delay, hydrocephalus and motor impairment.","explanation":"Neonatal bacterial meningitis can injure cochlear and cerebral structures, leaving long-term neurologic sequelae.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"44a49127b8cf94fc74a10c24d285f1de8a11192b6d994e112fa549525a773226","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-91b022bf94da":{"correct":"","answerText":"Poor feeding, altered activity/lethargy and fever or hypothermia.","explanation":"Young infants with meningitis may have nonspecific signs, sometimes with seizures or a bulging fontanelle.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ecc6a0b6be6fb60c6f5910d08f2c19f5eaaf6843d0a7a9d7bf6e1af1fd4db3d3","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-14fd00adb919":{"correct":"","answerText":"Ensure scene safety, check responsiveness, call for help/AED, assess breathing, start high-quality CPR when indicated, and use an AED as soon as available.","explanation":"Adult BLS emphasizes compressions of 100–120/min with adequate depth and minimal pauses; details differ by age and professional training.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ae1c184bad86f2a16dc2601b7d3f77fc457fdbffb6c543fdf7a72b43ea385534","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-1e03c08ad9b6":{"correct":"","answerText":"Levothyroxine replacement, titrated to trimester-specific TSH goals.","explanation":"Adequate maternal T4 is essential for fetal neural development; serum TSH is monitored and thyroid hormone requirements often rise in pregnancy.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e61e1243227c47de36e0393a7e34919ae66081bca3bed21fc5df989aa783907d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-d47cba21d9ca":{"correct":"","answerText":"Land, labor, capital and entrepreneurship.","explanation":"Economics commonly groups resources used in production into natural resources, human effort, physical/financial capital and organizing/innovating activity.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_written_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"212e8956f75d7819b4bc529eb2d72f756789a62f1480789868eb2557e77f0c05","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-9477204b5072":{"correct":"A","answerText":"fl uid mosaic model","explanation":"The plasma membrane is described by the fluid mosaic model: lipids and many proteins have lateral mobility in a dynamic bilayer, rather than a rigid mosaic.","optionReasons":{"A":"The plasma membrane is described by the fluid mosaic model: lipids and many proteins have lateral mobility in a dynamic bilayer, rather than a rigid mosaic."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"64728cfeb39ccbcbbc535a4371c11efe564a0b12a4c5d54deed051bfe1ca3359","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-d3b36bc973c3":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Transcription","explanation":"Transcription uses DNA as a template to synthesize an RNA transcript. Translation is the subsequent use of mRNA to synthesize protein.","optionReasons":{"B":"Transcription uses DNA as a template to synthesize an RNA transcript. Translation is the subsequent use of mRNA to synthesize protein."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1037ced67054bb2362e250f68d23bde1f1734b09aa41b70b87d6e326d100b652","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-5bf4fc57a89e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"gluteus medius","explanation":"The term medius means intermediate in size, distinguishing gluteus medius from gluteus maximus and minimus; the other muscle names refer mainly to attachment, action or shape.","optionReasons":{"B":"The term medius means intermediate in size, distinguishing gluteus medius from gluteus maximus and minimus; the other muscle names refer mainly to attachment, action or shape."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a1b6426a63e078c16c25ca4b3dc1b962001d4f7a67ee5257b58d36ee88ff503b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-d8feb78ff453":{"correct":"B","answerText":"a proton","explanation":"A proton is a subatomic constituent of an atom and is therefore smaller than a typical atom, molecule or ion.","optionReasons":{"B":"A proton is a subatomic constituent of an atom and is therefore smaller than a typical atom, molecule or ion."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fe477d07f9dba4f0470733ed10500864370a9d089b344ac94bf8050bbc750326","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-0a354b4bad14":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Secondary structure","explanation":"A helix is a regular local arrangement of the polypeptide backbone and is a secondary-structure element stabilized primarily by hydrogen bonds.","optionReasons":{"B":"A helix is a regular local arrangement of the polypeptide backbone and is a secondary-structure element stabilized primarily by hydrogen bonds."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f4dc06630218366d527503578daf3499253a46b2d299d2288cb68dd481466634","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f498fbae923b":{"correct":"B","answerText":"pyloric sphincter","explanation":"The pyloric sphincter is made of smooth muscle, whereas diaphragm, vastus lateralis and tongue contain skeletal muscle.","optionReasons":{"B":"The pyloric sphincter is made of smooth muscle, whereas diaphragm, vastus lateralis and tongue contain skeletal muscle."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b31a6838d78e2ab88d877ff12ecbf539fb1a5827c778c0fc37a1574b3be044a2","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-87807cf1f8fb":{"correct":"C","answerText":"stratum corneum","explanation":"The stratum corneum consists of keratinized dead cells and is the outermost epidermal layer of the skin.","optionReasons":{"C":"The stratum corneum consists of keratinized dead cells and is the outermost epidermal layer of the skin."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dc5f1cc3cf0673e9c3793906d6b61b53bf3c0729aa063b6808867bcc1c61b351","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-62567fb60525":{"correct":"D","answerText":"a, b, and c are correct","explanation":"Ovaries produce oocytes and secrete estrogens, progesterone and inhibins; therefore all three listed functions are correct.","optionReasons":{"D":"Ovaries produce oocytes and secrete estrogens, progesterone and inhibins; therefore all three listed functions are correct."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3d7070c16fe0917e993a09ce12f10f97b2079f88c45e8389515816a25823b843","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-48c06f00f139":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Aldosterone","explanation":"Aldosterone increases distal-nephron sodium reabsorption; water retention follows if water is available. ADH chiefly increases free-water reabsorption.","optionReasons":{"C":"Aldosterone increases distal-nephron sodium reabsorption; water retention follows if water is available. ADH chiefly increases free-water reabsorption."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"364579c92665cf0eaa88ee7ee148c68e28730b17fd62f47027404a225c2972e5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-be492c05a2c6":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Carbon and Hydrogen atoms","explanation":"A hydrocarbon is a chemical compound composed only of carbon and hydrogen atoms; oxygenated compounds are not pure hydrocarbons.","optionReasons":{"B":"A hydrocarbon is a chemical compound composed only of carbon and hydrogen atoms; oxygenated compounds are not pure hydrocarbons."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e3eae0c7245d45f3fb672cc4f3678dfd9eea018350875ad6d7a46628f834320b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-46372e6f654b":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Hyoid bone","explanation":"The hyoid is suspended by muscles and ligaments in the neck and does not normally articulate directly with another bone.","optionReasons":{"B":"The hyoid is suspended by muscles and ligaments in the neck and does not normally articulate directly with another bone."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4d7a9e2422c4491c27ea9406d634de56d60b863af83f8805313f2fbc3d0b026e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-73de76811a9b":{"correct":"A","answerText":"on the sternum","explanation":"The xiphoid process is the small inferior part of the sternum, not a structure of the arm, skull or leg.","optionReasons":{"A":"The xiphoid process is the small inferior part of the sternum, not a structure of the arm, skull or leg."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7d39e154521c011380f41c6e1a4a157ca371ab806402eff7244d34619330bc42","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-2026dfa9951c":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Cervical vertebrae","explanation":"The cervical vertebral column contains seven vertebrae C1–C7. The wrist normally has eight carpals and there are five lumbar vertebrae.","optionReasons":{"A":"The cervical vertebral column contains seven vertebrae C1–C7. The wrist normally has eight carpals and there are five lumbar vertebrae."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b3556acd0903165d34499c4867ff7dad082b6d5d9a5b963647bcc76e2193fe58","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-448051bb81e7":{"correct":"B","answerText":"homeostasis","explanation":"Homeostasis denotes regulation of the body's internal environment around physiological ranges through coordinated control systems.","optionReasons":{"B":"Homeostasis denotes regulation of the body's internal environment around physiological ranges through coordinated control systems."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"970563028c900d4615d8e9c675fea44d0480a3a732e20a8c15b529d6284564c9","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a1b778ef7a17":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Succinylcholine","explanation":"Succinylcholine is a depolarizing neuromuscular blocker; vecuronium is nondepolarizing, and scopolamine is antimuscarinic.","optionReasons":{"C":"Succinylcholine is a depolarizing neuromuscular blocker; vecuronium is nondepolarizing, and scopolamine is antimuscarinic."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8def383a771c951d0574cbd7e98e6a34d1c138eb326f4824b5b9e1eeb961e75a","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-aa4a4d573875":{"correct":"D","answerText":"nucleotide","explanation":"A nucleotide contains base, pentose sugar and phosphate. A nucleoside has only base and sugar.","optionReasons":{"D":"A nucleotide contains base, pentose sugar and phosphate. A nucleoside has only base and sugar."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e000073d58abae4fbb25c2e139700f0fbfade5d8ec424c30b32e0056231dc043","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-0eff363f36aa":{"correct":"A","answerText":"stratum corneum","explanation":"The stratum corneum is the superficial keratinized layer of the epidermis, above the other listed layers.","optionReasons":{"A":"The stratum corneum is the superficial keratinized layer of the epidermis, above the other listed layers."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c6d4cdbacb16fc3983e75a6e12c56e7b05002cb67512dbfdee606f062a1faf3e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-62143a5422e1":{"correct":"B","answerText":"clavicle, fibula, metatarsal, phalange, radius","explanation":"Clavicle, fibula, metatarsals, phalanges and radius are all parts of the appendicular skeleton; the other lists mix in axial bones.","optionReasons":{"B":"Clavicle, fibula, metatarsals, phalanges and radius are all parts of the appendicular skeleton; the other lists mix in axial bones."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"cca7911487af9ed9ce835e44e1d57b9c54781ce6cef1f2a756b877267ce1550b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-11a15aa8c41a":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Medial geniculate body","explanation":"The medial geniculate body is part of the auditory pathway; the lateral geniculate body, retina, optic nerve and chiasm belong to the visual pathway.","optionReasons":{"D":"The medial geniculate body is part of the auditory pathway; the lateral geniculate body, retina, optic nerve and chiasm belong to the visual pathway."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"2407d81daa50b91de39c2176f5e8d4664cdf0dbd520b36d15f76ec54fe5724f9","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-76dee63a59c6":{"correct":"C","answerText":"trabeculum","explanation":"Trabeculae are internal struts of cancellous bone, whereas trochanters, tubercles and tuberosities are surface prominences.","optionReasons":{"C":"Trabeculae are internal struts of cancellous bone, whereas trochanters, tubercles and tuberosities are surface prominences."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dca735d31747707ab163ea5c475b2592aec2651b8df13da919b92269f94c924e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-95361757c458":{"correct":"C","answerText":"pelvis","explanation":"The acetabulum is the socket in the hip (coxal) bone that articulates with the femoral head.","optionReasons":{"C":"The acetabulum is the socket in the hip (coxal) bone that articulates with the femoral head."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"281e71d2fc2b7383b6026a54b00b55d047343eaff1555b36179735ef8b942539","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-886f0b58b4e5":{"correct":"D","answerText":"AV anastomoses","explanation":"An arteriovenous anastomosis is a direct communication between arteries and veins, bypassing part of the capillary network.","optionReasons":{"D":"An arteriovenous anastomosis is a direct communication between arteries and veins, bypassing part of the capillary network."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3fe6287cd1c1e0902910bdf008fb4623342601e4b7caef4c27f81b5e7e04e6b5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-67fc8fa2ff00":{"correct":"A","answerText":"there is fl uid between the articulating bones","explanation":"A synovial joint has a joint cavity containing synovial fluid between articular surfaces; it need not be a ball-and-socket joint.","optionReasons":{"A":"A synovial joint has a joint cavity containing synovial fluid between articular surfaces; it need not be a ball-and-socket joint."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a1f803b14cf38157d8d96c593c7a2a80c2d962e5b11d44164c678a3b6f418e05","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7671b4eca9c4":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Propylthiouracil","explanation":"Propylthiouracil is an antithyroid drug that may be used in pregnancy, especially in the first trimester when indicated; valproate, warfarin and tetracyclines carry important fetal risks.","optionReasons":{"A":"Propylthiouracil is an antithyroid drug that may be used in pregnancy, especially in the first trimester when indicated; valproate, warfarin and tetracyclines carry important fetal risks."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1313733928d4173ee570a724cc91da2f445bb210d058d1b672c04af7fe0d9c48","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a29770984219":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Loperamide","explanation":"Loperamide activates peripheral mu-opioid receptors in the gut, slowing intestinal motility; the other options are laxatives.","optionReasons":{"C":"Loperamide activates peripheral mu-opioid receptors in the gut, slowing intestinal motility; the other options are laxatives."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6fc1f26256471fa6d3afcb0c08a24a9d9d5ce588d3b9f09b76ddffb1ac913b03","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-86ef4c4df7eb":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Antidiuretic property","explanation":"Vasopressin acts on V2 receptors in collecting ducts to increase aquaporin-mediated water reabsorption; it also causes vasoconstriction through V1 receptors.","optionReasons":{"A":"Vasopressin acts on V2 receptors in collecting ducts to increase aquaporin-mediated water reabsorption; it also causes vasoconstriction through V1 receptors."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"af319cd59871d5cee73e91953ba8b4acbe591baafd6a6a2966485bf4123e85fe","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-79363ad06383":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Alcohol dehydrogenase","explanation":"Fomepizole competitively inhibits alcohol dehydrogenase, preventing formation of toxic metabolites of methanol and ethylene glycol.","optionReasons":{"C":"Fomepizole competitively inhibits alcohol dehydrogenase, preventing formation of toxic metabolites of methanol and ethylene glycol."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d8d7f08e54f0172d4c34e57f04f328d02f913cdf23195e9ff5a08943d37548ce","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7a20402575ac":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Morphine","explanation":"Morphine is a strong mu-opioid receptor agonist. Naloxone is an antagonist and pentazocine/buprenorphine have different partial or mixed agonist profiles.","optionReasons":{"B":"Morphine is a strong mu-opioid receptor agonist. Naloxone is an antagonist and pentazocine/buprenorphine have different partial or mixed agonist profiles."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8555b396036b98e666ccc52681f3bd8932c08c91fb5f43677bd9a8c7e4de38d4","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e50a5a56a019":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Protamine sulfate","explanation":"Protamine sulfate is positively charged and complexes with negatively charged heparin to reverse its anticoagulant effect.","optionReasons":{"D":"Protamine sulfate is positively charged and complexes with negatively charged heparin to reverse its anticoagulant effect."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"878519668e26f41b3dd4783ec5efc9bd776b3ba8e8bb7d8547b9240b1e7d66e0","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4bfa27604231":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Skin rash","explanation":"Skin rash is a common early hypersensitivity reaction to penicillins; serious allergy is less common but must be recognized.","optionReasons":{"E":"Skin rash is a common early hypersensitivity reaction to penicillins; serious allergy is less common but must be recognized."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c9e0f101904cdc242b4686f94054f8392d8f2cc0c5f1f84d9db53ebfe9bbcbc8","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-46a0a732bd9d":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Haptenes","explanation":"Many small drug molecules act as haptens: after binding host proteins they can be recognized as immunogenic conjugates.","optionReasons":{"B":"Many small drug molecules act as haptens: after binding host proteins they can be recognized as immunogenic conjugates."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"88de647b327cdcd7183b85a2eaff46ceb643adbdfbdfe33e7b50cf0bbe963856","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-131204700008":{"correct":"B","answerText":"IgM.","explanation":"T-independent antigens, particularly polysaccharides, usually elicit mainly IgM and comparatively poor class switching and memory.","optionReasons":{"B":"T-independent antigens, particularly polysaccharides, usually elicit mainly IgM and comparatively poor class switching and memory."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f61c6896f560491f8358131e33b53ee869f5721af79769d8d087ae4c7af533ee","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c99301485969":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Nucleocapsid","explanation":"Both enveloped and non-enveloped viruses possess a nucleocapsid; a lipid envelope is specific to enveloped virions.","optionReasons":{"A":"Both enveloped and non-enveloped viruses possess a nucleocapsid; a lipid envelope is specific to enveloped virions."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5bc10aa7d4d50445eeff14a965874325911a53294be82f8d18d0d382c06e155d","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-d22660a47a93":{"correct":"D","answerText":"protect from disease upon re-infection with a specific pathogen.","explanation":"Adaptive immunity generates antigen-specific lymphocytes and immunological memory, allowing stronger responses after re-exposure.","optionReasons":{"D":"Adaptive immunity generates antigen-specific lymphocytes and immunological memory, allowing stronger responses after re-exposure."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3ff16b8ee24a9c9c156d1b9c8c90e867a411409eef2db4d2ac35061b59ba60ac","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e0eab9ffd6ce":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Staphylococcus","explanation":"Staphylococci are catalase-positive aerobic Gram-positive cocci; typical streptococci and enterococci lack catalase activity.","optionReasons":{"C":"Staphylococci are catalase-positive aerobic Gram-positive cocci; typical streptococci and enterococci lack catalase activity."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ec7b9444396b1d6fff12be3a7ae98995345429ec737e01160a4eec607f6d2289","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-566f256cf80e":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Capsule","explanation":"Bacillus anthracis has an antiphagocytic poly-D-glutamate capsule, allowing vegetative cells to resist phagocytosis.","optionReasons":{"D":"Bacillus anthracis has an antiphagocytic poly-D-glutamate capsule, allowing vegetative cells to resist phagocytosis."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8574ce0e7858fc5da62d5e44d9f45009a7adcfc19565d495e606b373a7c4e3c6","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-290acfcd8ba1":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Escherichia","explanation":"Escherichia coli is the leading Enterobacteriaceae cause of community-acquired urinary tract infection.","optionReasons":{"A":"Escherichia coli is the leading Enterobacteriaceae cause of community-acquired urinary tract infection."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"75e1b7862b3334f585ef9c3a699953f61f8fa8f26bbf5b6cc6f75d2b3cc7dfd9","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-0eeafc37092e":{"correct":"E","answerText":"in acidified endosomes.","explanation":"Exogenous proteins are taken into acidified endosomal/lysosomal compartments and processed for loading onto MHC class II molecules.","optionReasons":{"E":"Exogenous proteins are taken into acidified endosomal/lysosomal compartments and processed for loading onto MHC class II molecules."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"110e70c3b3d3b7fa8f45fdff7a8c84b0097dee0e663c52bfe71cb64a421b1cda","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-6ccf935cd6ff":{"correct":"E","answerText":"TAP-1 and TAP-2.","explanation":"TAP1 and TAP2 transport cytosolic peptides into the endoplasmic reticulum for presentation by MHC class I.","optionReasons":{"E":"TAP1 and TAP2 transport cytosolic peptides into the endoplasmic reticulum for presentation by MHC class I."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0dc195129a712acb9009852409ba596c9b99c50722a989fd9c0cffa37881b958","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e84a1a8af162":{"correct":"D","answerText":"histamine.","explanation":"Histamine is a preformed mediator in mast-cell granules and acts rapidly to increase vascular permeability and trigger allergic symptoms.","optionReasons":{"D":"Histamine is a preformed mediator in mast-cell granules and acts rapidly to increase vascular permeability and trigger allergic symptoms."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5a650971c92b0cef37ebc058be58af9a17853f2b038cbc1cc15c3087a3f6db85","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a694ac2e73ac":{"correct":"B","answerText":"capable of developing into any blood cells.","explanation":"Multipotent hematopoietic stem cells can form all mature blood cell lineages, including erythroid, myeloid and lymphoid cells.","optionReasons":{"B":"Multipotent hematopoietic stem cells can form all mature blood cell lineages, including erythroid, myeloid and lymphoid cells."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d83b45efb102f238704253402c430b01f550b1be88e3ac056f71c8c120d3b773","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-dc9b50a7ac50":{"correct":"A","answerText":"becomes inactivated.","explanation":"Recognition of antigen without adequate costimulation can induce T-cell anergy, a mechanism of peripheral tolerance.","optionReasons":{"A":"Recognition of antigen without adequate costimulation can induce T-cell anergy, a mechanism of peripheral tolerance."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"82238659a491e1fa22cc1d3eb67abab232a5b21c2c7783a1f3c9ad369eb536d3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ef757050820e":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Atypical pneumonia","explanation":"Legionella pneumophila is a cause of atypical pneumonia, often with extrapulmonary manifestations; it is not a usual cause of urinary tract infection.","optionReasons":{"C":"Legionella pneumophila is a cause of atypical pneumonia, often with extrapulmonary manifestations; it is not a usual cause of urinary tract infection."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"42bad3529c9eb41f84ee5acde3bcc548d4977630ba3e324ab83937e4020956c4","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-89497d2fa3be":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Varicella-zoster virus (VZV)","explanation":"Live attenuated varicella-zoster vaccines have existed; there are no established routine live-attenuated vaccines for the other herpesviruses listed.","optionReasons":{"C":"Live attenuated varicella-zoster vaccines have existed; there are no established routine live-attenuated vaccines for the other herpesviruses listed."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c9911e4c4d045354793a27ea824867e9b34e5062f9e5e9083612a4346c989723","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-9916aa09cb8e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"C3b.","explanation":"C3b is an important opsonin recognized by complement receptors on neutrophils and macrophages, enhancing phagocytosis.","optionReasons":{"B":"C3b is an important opsonin recognized by complement receptors on neutrophils and macrophages, enhancing phagocytosis."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"485c69dc06614fc72b13583b827975cfeb5a9c7cf36f7213ddd77ad9fe33884e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-030d2fddd197":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Epstein-Barr virus (EBV)","explanation":"Infectious mononucleosis due to EBV characteristically produces atypical reactive CD8 T lymphocytes (Downey cells).","optionReasons":{"A":"Infectious mononucleosis due to EBV characteristically produces atypical reactive CD8 T lymphocytes (Downey cells)."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"32ac2b08a3ab6861450e4cf82a23de0a7d3ccccd70a79f6eee38d50795cd1a81","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-2ce7062534cb":{"correct":"B","answerText":"the protein be recognized by helper T cells.","explanation":"A carrier protein supplies peptide epitopes presented to helper T cells; hapten-specific B cells then receive help to produce anti-hapten antibody.","optionReasons":{"B":"A carrier protein supplies peptide epitopes presented to helper T cells; hapten-specific B cells then receive help to produce anti-hapten antibody."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"119339fd8a853cbb8e55f382e47e6de1b44f13f5692e46fc9710305dfe2502ac","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-0855fafe6062":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Toxic Shock Syndrome (TSS) and Scarlet fever","explanation":"Group A streptococcal pyrogenic exotoxins are superantigens implicated in scarlet fever and streptococcal toxic shock syndrome.","optionReasons":{"C":"Group A streptococcal pyrogenic exotoxins are superantigens implicated in scarlet fever and streptococcal toxic shock syndrome."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d832c4809aada1e0357d7e1f4575adba652d72b9a3d05bb659d17ab4eb218918","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ca9ce7ab0c2f":{"correct":"B","answerText":"increased numbers of severe bacterial infections.","explanation":"C3 deficiency impairs opsonization and complement amplification, causing recurrent severe pyogenic bacterial infections.","optionReasons":{"B":"C3 deficiency impairs opsonization and complement amplification, causing recurrent severe pyogenic bacterial infections."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d25461a9d942f3692c7b05af25d8b37de1d11574f2ee0b7e0882f8dcc3376e16","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ea6dea36e771":{"correct":"C","answerText":"They will cross the placenta and fix complement.","explanation":"IgE does not cross the placenta efficiently and is not a classical complement-fixing immunoglobulin; IgG provides transplacental antibody.","optionReasons":{"C":"IgE does not cross the placenta efficiently and is not a classical complement-fixing immunoglobulin; IgG provides transplacental antibody."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d394b3fdb11df459b00ab527188d4dbe94513a99ecd9e8d9dc096272486f72e6","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-cb52054e8d50":{"correct":"C","answerText":"initiated by haptens.","explanation":"Penicillin hypersensitivity and poison-oak contact dermatitis can both be triggered by haptens, although their immune mechanisms differ.","optionReasons":{"C":"Penicillin hypersensitivity and poison-oak contact dermatitis can both be triggered by haptens, although their immune mechanisms differ."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9f17db1b4a8a6967f96705189f6fd45799f323fad3b57e50a6c457c090b314dc","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4c20ee90942e":{"correct":"A","answerText":"a single terminal sugar residue.","explanation":"The ABO A and B determinants differ in terminal carbohydrate residues: A has N-acetylgalactosamine and B has galactose.","optionReasons":{"A":"The ABO A and B determinants differ in terminal carbohydrate residues: A has N-acetylgalactosamine and B has galactose."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fea1bf3e632b17256b1261b3d9ae9566f140ea2575869c3ea8b3050298cef270","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-732b4a3e368d":{"correct":"C","answerText":"an antigenic determinant is a paratope","explanation":"An antigenic determinant is an epitope; a paratope is the complementary antigen-binding region of an antibody or receptor.","optionReasons":{"C":"An antigenic determinant is an epitope; a paratope is the complementary antigen-binding region of an antibody or receptor."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"38a67ff9090731138b2fe739bed5f27bac7cda8a41221e3db0fc74aa3efdd32c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-043c970c8bba":{"correct":"D","answerText":"is determined by the heavy chain type","explanation":"Antibody class (IgM, IgG, IgA, etc.) is determined by the heavy-chain constant region type, not its light chain or antigen.","optionReasons":{"D":"Antibody class (IgM, IgG, IgA, etc.) is determined by the heavy-chain constant region type, not its light chain or antigen."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"344cc232df63c0c09b19921d47d26666e00765f7aadefa5f45a4fc6f17d76110","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-35743551ac42":{"correct":"C","answerText":"present antigen for recognition by the T-cell antigen receptor","explanation":"MHC molecules present peptide antigens for recognition by alpha-beta T-cell receptors, while coreceptors help establish CD4/CD8 specificity.","optionReasons":{"C":"MHC molecules present peptide antigens for recognition by alpha-beta T-cell receptors, while coreceptors help establish CD4/CD8 specificity."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bbf8f81a87c35136bfb1dcd732b85c6591022eff6143b7a506e827d3e261c655","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-279368473752":{"correct":"A","answerText":"interleukin-1","explanation":"Interleukin-1 is mainly produced by antigen-presenting innate cells such as macrophages; activated helper T cells can produce IL-2, IL-4 and interferon-gamma depending on subset.","optionReasons":{"A":"Interleukin-1 is mainly produced by antigen-presenting innate cells such as macrophages; activated helper T cells can produce IL-2, IL-4 and interferon-gamma depending on subset."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"57fcf45941bb652e4a7e9aa47ed1a64490c32cb1994ea7ca0d505cc5e7a6cedf","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e0e8733306a2":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Glycosylated Hemoglobin","explanation":"HbA1c reflects glycation over the erythrocyte lifespan and is used to assess mean glycemic exposure over roughly two to three months.","optionReasons":{"A":"HbA1c reflects glycation over the erythrocyte lifespan and is used to assess mean glycemic exposure over roughly two to three months."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"106ac557da2778d24d38d60c6bd8d948461628eb561c08d84e86f542672ee8a5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-dae2fd543512":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Urine WBC Casts","explanation":"Rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis typically causes nephritic renal failure and glomerular crescents; WBC casts are more characteristic of interstitial inflammation/pyelonephritis.","optionReasons":{"D":"Rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis typically causes nephritic renal failure and glomerular crescents; WBC casts are more characteristic of interstitial inflammation/pyelonephritis."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c78bfe106dbe92965964f684c6598200045fdfa5cc8e0e1956c5a9212611d628","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-044f83fa85df":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Increased DNA synthesis","explanation":"Reversible cell injury reduces ATP, disrupts ion pumps and causes cellular swelling; increased DNA synthesis is not a characteristic injury mechanism.","optionReasons":{"A":"Reversible cell injury reduces ATP, disrupts ion pumps and causes cellular swelling; increased DNA synthesis is not a characteristic injury mechanism."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8737bf8092a727149566a8c44a58b65d23143fa2f9e178414c88f72170264222","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4e2950b0cff4":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Caeseating Granuloma","explanation":"Sarcoidosis characteristically produces noncaseating granulomas, whereas caseating granulomas suggest other causes such as tuberculosis.","optionReasons":{"C":"Sarcoidosis characteristically produces noncaseating granulomas, whereas caseating granulomas suggest other causes such as tuberculosis."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f0ec4b255f6a46a7f075e10f7d3faf5f810e4e6580b9b92d9a85cdbde4aba678","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-35185c403921":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Polymorphonuclear Leukocytes","explanation":"Mature granulomas are macrophage- and epithelioid-cell-rich with giant cells/lymphocytes; neutrophils are not their defining cellular population.","optionReasons":{"C":"Mature granulomas are macrophage- and epithelioid-cell-rich with giant cells/lymphocytes; neutrophils are not their defining cellular population."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"2609d13d667fd3f076919cb587acee02bfa7bc3022d66daccf649a7cc121b1e3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f78ef2865a04":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Rupture of the spleen","explanation":"Infectious mononucleosis can cause splenomegaly and splenic rupture, a rare but important complication.","optionReasons":{"C":"Infectious mononucleosis can cause splenomegaly and splenic rupture, a rare but important complication."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4aadb33bd7bda0d48d62c8944f0b52274484391e08a012b06d67c7d8cd22b876","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a7da63f6a469":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Carcinoma of Vulva","explanation":"Persistent high-risk HPV infections are strongly associated with squamous neoplasia of the vulva, cervix and other anogenital sites.","optionReasons":{"E":"Persistent high-risk HPV infections are strongly associated with squamous neoplasia of the vulva, cervix and other anogenital sites."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"aff00ebbe9f6deab546df7de1bcadfc267f8d510f42210902f33fece1996e15d","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-165f4bece070":{"correct":"E","answerText":"arrhythmia","explanation":"Cardiac arrhythmias are the most common early complication of myocardial infarction, reflecting electrical instability of ischemic myocardium.","optionReasons":{"E":"Cardiac arrhythmias are the most common early complication of myocardial infarction, reflecting electrical instability of ischemic myocardium."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"32daf6c92f83d2fab1ea26e91108903332e17f4b3960abb58d3e6a7e3d9ef3f2","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a806e0e453c9":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis","explanation":"Ulcerative colitis is strongly associated with primary sclerosing cholangitis, a chronic inflammatory cholangiopathy.","optionReasons":{"D":"Ulcerative colitis is strongly associated with primary sclerosing cholangitis, a chronic inflammatory cholangiopathy."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"90f43ba03a1ac9ca283f235ec219b41580825c8ebfba401d7a2121f8e87bfe99","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ba9891b3a760":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Diphyllobothrium Latum Infection","explanation":"Fish-tapeworm infection (Diphyllobothrium/Dibothriocephalus) classically causes vitamin B12 deficiency rather than folate deficiency.","optionReasons":{"D":"Fish-tapeworm infection (Diphyllobothrium/Dibothriocephalus) classically causes vitamin B12 deficiency rather than folate deficiency."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a08229061cc24b2c3195609ff1b0f9e585ad4a76198df5d7995c391cf0d24645","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-12946e094ba4":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Hepar Lobatum","explanation":"Hepar lobatum is a late manifestation of tertiary syphilis and is not a typical feature of secondary syphilis.","optionReasons":{"D":"Hepar lobatum is a late manifestation of tertiary syphilis and is not a typical feature of secondary syphilis."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"aef3537c8556cf647158577da87f7d61e3a9083782324cdc06b3b90112be3191","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a428a7ebc13f":{"correct":"A","answerText":"characterized by RS cells in histological section","explanation":"Classical Hodgkin lymphoma is identified by Reed–Sternberg-type tumor cells in the appropriate inflammatory histologic background.","optionReasons":{"A":"Classical Hodgkin lymphoma is identified by Reed–Sternberg-type tumor cells in the appropriate inflammatory histologic background."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c5c2