37","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e3ae7bbe4c43":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Adhesive disk","explanation":"Giardia trophozoites attach to small bowel mucosa using their characteristic ventral adhesive disc.","optionReasons":{"A":"Giardia trophozoites attach to small bowel mucosa using their characteristic ventral adhesive disc."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"2427ef4a0fa13532cdcf12185bb25bccbe4732f06213dbcf87ac42db6b6bd072","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-34ee9726bcc7":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Caecum","explanation":"Adult Trichuris trichiura (whipworms) attach to the cecal/colonic mucosa.","optionReasons":{"D":"Adult Trichuris trichiura (whipworms) attach to the cecal/colonic mucosa."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9d767905f68056f5ef1e01a7e3bbcc0addce6e497d0a01c21f003c39d603954b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-5f8e43f6b753":{"correct":"C","answerText":"gametocytes","explanation":"Female Anopheles mosquitoes ingest gametocytes during a blood meal; sexual development then proceeds in the mosquito.","optionReasons":{"C":"Female Anopheles mosquitoes ingest gametocytes during a blood meal; sexual development then proceeds in the mosquito."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b52e1d823c6f666c209f49d550d6580515845db2c3b0976aee0f0c97b18b7ca8","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ead5b3d09dd7":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Cercariae","explanation":"Schistosoma cercariae released by freshwater snails penetrate the skin and represent the human-infective stage.","optionReasons":{"B":"Schistosoma cercariae released by freshwater snails penetrate the skin and represent the human-infective stage."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6292db1ae7c1f5fba2e8500976db7060df220c52cb4d1b7e0705c4264f3b66ec","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7ad3d132c55a":{"correct":"D","answerText":"median body, ventral groove, binucleate","explanation":"Giardia trophozoites have two nuclei, ventral attachment disc/groove and median bodies, distinguishing them from trypanosomes and apicomplexans.","optionReasons":{"D":"Giardia trophozoites have two nuclei, ventral attachment disc/groove and median bodies, distinguishing them from trypanosomes and apicomplexans."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f89c8f3f16fec4e116d6b0758984fd69f2cce812be516cb09f3f0ba0d15f1042","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-63fec7e4eb11":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Bulinus globosus","explanation":"Bulinus snails are intermediate hosts for Schistosoma haematobium, whereas Biomphalaria snails transmit S. mansoni.","optionReasons":{"B":"Bulinus snails are intermediate hosts for Schistosoma haematobium, whereas Biomphalaria snails transmit S. mansoni."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8211b62522c4607c235fcee5a63b268f086b6c21216fac20ee4aa3346e523d52","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-24da2d3aa744":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Fresh water fish","explanation":"The fish tapeworm uses a freshwater fish as its second intermediate 