ccessive intermediate hosts.","optionReasons":{"C":"Diphyllobothrium/Dibothriocephalus uses copepods and freshwater fish as successive intermediate hosts."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fd173c08e717890e9def6c98391f0e55674e07beacfab60b78a8b2dfe7f2e1e3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-94265555d7eb":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Presence of Maurer’s dots","explanation":"Maurer's clefts/dots are associated with Plasmodium falciparum-infected red cells; P. vivax typically shows Schüffner stippling.","optionReasons":{"E":"Maurer's clefts/dots are associated with Plasmodium falciparum-infected red cells; P. vivax typically shows Schüffner stippling."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fdde4ec8ad21eeefcb70aca833f52ba7286f4031043abef6a9586dc01f60027c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a747a3eace43":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Normal inspiration expands the thoracic cavity through rib elevation and outward movement plus diaphragm descent.","optionReasons":{"D":"Normal inspiration expands the thoracic cavity through rib elevation and outward movement plus diaphragm descent."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"061dd1583527f40cc52f8ebdde78fd9a20f2be0dca54efac6c8620b9c12e6a25","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e8b6f2280fee":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Lower pons","explanation":"The traditional apneustic region is described in the lower pons, contributing to inspiratory drive and patterning.","optionReasons":{"B":"The traditional apneustic region is described in the lower pons, contributing to inspiratory drive and patterning."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"72e9f3cf9df798a615e9fdc4c8fdc21afcaea868aeebce414cb1eb414bafe29a","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c39b7155055e":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Hypoxic hypoxia","explanation":"Hypoxic hypoxia results from reduced arterial oxygen tension (PaO2), not primarily reduced hemoglobin amount or tissue blood flow.","optionReasons":{"A":"Hypoxic hypoxia results from reduced arterial oxygen tension (PaO2), not primarily reduced hemoglobin amount or tissue blood flow."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"38ce29152e029092430c1fc88e6d1aa12816037176cdc9d679fc2225af9460b2","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-08ebe19abbb2":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Scoliosis","explanation":"Scoliosis can cause restrictive physiology with reduced vital capacity while the FEV1/FVC ratio may remain normal.","optionReasons":{"B":"Scoliosis can cause restrictive physiology with reduced vital capacity while the FEV1/FVC ratio may remain normal."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_curated_option_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"714ac08279127e97b0c220a4618c4fda2745e60168ff6d6853a37810f05dec48","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-60b72166eee5":{"correct":"D","answerText":"They have opposite physiological effects (p. 49)","explanation":"Physiological antagonists act at different receptors or pathways but have opposing biological effects; epinephrine can oppose histamine-induced bronc