ncy is the most frequent cause of anemia in pregnancy because maternal iron requirements rise substantially.","optionReasons":{"A":"Iron deficiency is the most frequent cause of anemia in pregnancy because maternal iron requirements rise substantially."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_narrow_concept_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f450671595d62366c4f87e2c4d1318ff9a6aa2d1b2007647fe66066acd2d99b8","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-73db705b88be":{"correct":"A","answerText":"20004.2","explanation":"The arithmetic mean is (2 + 3 + 7 + 9 + 100000)/5 = 20004.2; a large outlier heavily increases the mean.","optionReasons":{"A":"The arithmetic mean is (2 + 3 + 7 + 9 + 100000)/5 = 20004.2; a large outlier heavily increases the mean."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_narrow_concept_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ee074fdf1f2d5ebc480b40df9859c89f38c142c279ff05836d1f2c551c795338","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c8db835a3fb7":{"correct":"C","answerText":"7","explanation":"After ordering 2, 3, 7, 9, 100000, the middle of five values is 7, showing resistance to the outlier.","optionReasons":{"C":"After ordering 2, 3, 7, 9, 100000, the middle of five values is 7, showing resistance to the outlier."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_narrow_concept_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f5a656bf7575f37c3c0c578fbb4cfc28d9560978ed164099808743dcbc662ef0","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-183df10fd802":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Mother to child transmission (MTCT)","explanation":"Most HIV infections in young children are acquired vertically during pregnancy, delivery or breastfeeding.","optionReasons":{"A":"Most HIV infections in young children are acquired vertically during pregnancy, delivery or breastfeeding."},"references":[],"review":"original_key_excluded_independently_reasoned_narrow_concept_review","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c7b764b424b18742a8600ef02e674e22168719c88a9aafab8fa809f7134cbfcc","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-b03bcfe3761f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"AV anastomoses","explanation":"An arteriovenous anastomosis is a direct communication between arteries and veins, bypassing part of the capillary network.","optionReasons":{"D":"An arteriovenous anastomosis is a direct communication between arteries and veins, bypassing part of the capillary network."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_newly_curated_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3fe6287cd1c1e0902910bdf008fb4623342601e4b7caef4c27f81b5e7e04e6b5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7ad937ce90fa":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Alcohol dehydrogenase","explanation":"Fomepizole competitively inhibits alcohol dehydrogenase, preventing formation of toxic metabolites of methanol and ethylene glycol.","optionReasons":{"C":"Fomepizole competitively inhibits alcohol dehydrogenase, preventing formation of toxic metabolites of methanol and ethylene glycol."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_newly_curated_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d8d7f08e54f0172d4c34e57f04f328d02f913cdf23195e9ff5a08943d37548ce","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a12ff4ef96eb":{"correct":"D","answerText":"nucleotide","explanation":"A nucleotide contains base, pentose sugar and phosphate. A nucleoside has only base and sugar.","optionReasons":{"D":"A nucleotide contains base, pentose sugar and phosphate. A nucleoside has only base and sugar."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_newly_curated_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e000073d58abae4fbb25c2e139700f0fbfade5d8ec424c30b32e0056231dc043","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-70c0f4ff7a55":{"correct":"B","answerText":"homeostasis","explanation":"Homeostasis denotes regulation of the body's internal environment around physiological ranges through coordinated control systems.","optionReasons":{"B":"Homeostasis denotes regulation of the body's internal environment around physiological ranges through coordinated control systems."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_newly_curated_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"970563028c900d4615d8e9c675fea44d0480a3a732e20a8c15b529d6284564c9","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-db1a493ee990":{"correct":"C","answerText":"trabeculum","explanation":"Trabeculae are internal struts of cancellous bone, whereas trochanters, tubercles and tuberosities are surface prominences.","optionReasons":{"C":"Trabeculae are internal struts of cancellous bone, whereas trochanters, tubercles and tuberosities are surface prominences."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_newly_curated_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dca735d31747707ab163ea5c475b2592aec2651b8df13da919b92269f94c924e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-1de84a435f87":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Range","explanation":"Range is a measure of spread, not central tendency; mean, median and mode all describe typical location.","optionReasons":{"B":"Range is a measure of spread, not central tendency; mean, median and mode all describe typical location."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_newly_curated_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"61baf282f1a29a9607becd77d7f5c4c60a029361ec11598f8435801fbd491ccd","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-6dc13e60b385":{"correct":"C","answerText":"trabeculum","explanation":"Trabeculae are internal struts of cancellous bone, whereas trochanters, tubercles and tuberosities are surface prominences.","optionReasons":{"C":"Trabeculae are internal struts of cancellous bone, whereas trochanters, tubercles and tuberosities are surface prominences."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_newly_curated_answer","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dca735d31747707ab163ea5c475b2592aec2651b8df13da919b92269f94c924e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a625f1af9067":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Muscle","explanation":"The liver has a venous portal system, the kidney an arterial portal arrangement, and the hypothalamic–pituitary system a portal circulation. Skeletal muscle does not have a conventional portal vascular system.","optionReasons":{"C":"The liver has a venous portal system, the kidney an arterial portal arrangement, and the hypothalamic–pituitary system a portal circulation. Skeletal muscle does not have a conventional portal vascular system."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"62ad15c6983536b7a2443cb6ddd1320681950148f36ec06cd8b04226da6e25f6","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-91cb39349f27":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Capillaries, arterioles, and post capillary venules","explanation":"The microcirculation encompasses arterioles, capillaries and postcapillary venules. Larger veins and arteries are not usually counted as the microvascular exchange bed.","optionReasons":{"C":"The microcirculation encompasses arterioles, capillaries and postcapillary venules. Larger veins and arteries are not usually counted as the microvascular exchange bed."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e9fb60da2f1043c534028842c006e63519fcad040c17440f55219624af93a1b9","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-149e7a51e645":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Sinusoidal capillaries","explanation":"Sinusoids are discontinuous, wide-lumen vessels with a relatively permeable endothelial lining, particularly in liver, spleen and marrow.","optionReasons":{"C":"Sinusoids are discontinuous, wide-lumen vessels with a relatively permeable endothelial lining, particularly in liver, spleen and marrow."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e2d1e6c9b47991fa517b789e612914dc68059738905fe7ef0518af5374fc2156","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e3437dc7a48e":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Kidney","explanation":"The renal glomerulus has an afferent arteriole, a capillary tuft and an efferent arteriole, constituting an arterial portal arrangement.","optionReasons":{"A":"The renal glomerulus has an afferent arteriole, a capillary tuft and an efferent arteriole, constituting an arterial portal arrangement."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d7e7b4d12b5a0a27aa88fa0ec0b2ad900c5f69b531fcdedf6695e85f9c8ae890","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-b9b1f43b4070":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Elastic artery","explanation":"The aorta is a conducting elastic artery with prominent elastic lamellae that smooth pulsatile cardiac ejection.","optionReasons":{"D":"The aorta is a conducting elastic artery with prominent elastic lamellae that smooth pulsatile cardiac ejection."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8b08cf95f024af4b599cee760130552b9b5d5222f53589b7471e535950920260","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-cb0527ab456e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Fenestrated capillaries","explanation":"Fenestrated capillaries contain fenestrae or pores through endothelial cells to facilitate transport; discontinuous sinusoids have larger gaps.","optionReasons":{"B":"Fenestrated capillaries contain fenestrae or pores through endothelial cells to facilitate transport; discontinuous sinusoids have larger gaps."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6d2c7b91f2f4b17730412fcee525dda0d0138ad25d70969e3d28d8185f19cbc3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-73c889f34aee":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Venule","explanation":"Blood leaves the capillary bed through postcapillary venules, which then converge into larger veins.","optionReasons":{"C":"Blood leaves the capillary bed through postcapillary venules, which then converge into larger veins."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b3ac511228eb931e72615e1ee463c19a9e23d721aa40c814332ecf90731ae8cc","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e9a4fdef30bc":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Venous sinus","explanation":"Dural venous sinuses are endothelial-lined venous channels between layers of the dura mater surrounding the brain.","optionReasons":{"E":"Dural venous sinuses are endothelial-lined venous channels between layers of the dura mater surrounding the brain."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b3678020d7ec4b31de255c5e98196e7669ee245509599355fb173d2c0c36a7c3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c62fa4a3a02f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"GALT","explanation":"GALT means gut-associated lymphoid tissue; intestinal lymphocytes and Peyer patches are examples.","optionReasons":{"D":"GALT means gut-associated lymphoid tissue; intestinal lymphocytes and Peyer patches are examples."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f57632a85c934d3621e532869a9757c34d476ce71fea9d1ddea26bb93138c3f9","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-60816cc147d3":{"correct":"E","answerText":"All of the above are functions of the spleen","explanation":"The spleen filters aged erythrocytes, supports lymphocyte responses, serves as a blood reservoir to varying degrees and is a fetal hematopoietic organ.","optionReasons":{"E":"The spleen filters aged erythrocytes, supports lymphocyte responses, serves as a blood reservoir to varying degrees and is a fetal hematopoietic organ."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1c940a6dcbc8ded90f4087cfdb91fc8b0fca5c1a750c1d3e996ccf64bf4497d0","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7f68689a6100":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Germinal center","explanation":"A secondary lymphoid follicle is identified by a germinal center formed following antigenic activation and B-cell proliferation.","optionReasons":{"A":"A secondary lymphoid follicle is identified by a germinal center formed following antigenic activation and B-cell proliferation."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"30660e0a78c1f745a3f5721cefe8186dd78eac14bd1ca7febf502c1e28a7629f","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-d031979f9d33":{"correct":"A","answerText":"BALT","explanation":"BALT stands for bronchus-associated lymphoid tissue, a component of mucosa-associated immunity along the respiratory tract.","optionReasons":{"A":"BALT stands for bronchus-associated lymphoid tissue, a component of mucosa-associated immunity along the respiratory tract."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"923fc3f73b70e0ec6ae37ea1834110e59e9576b5363d1f516e007a4fec4d8f0c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c1b95b2d778e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"White pulp","explanation":"The spleen’s white pulp comprises lymphoid tissue around central arterioles and associated follicles.","optionReasons":{"B":"The spleen’s white pulp comprises lymphoid tissue around central arterioles and associated follicles."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c7e810839c71c8b8828b7fcbb8424f3f8b318d3bab1c6894d3673e83bcfa2c25","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-b3c32b48b588":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Cords of Billroth","explanation":"Splenic cords of Billroth are cellular meshworks in the red pulp between the venous sinuses.","optionReasons":{"A":"Splenic cords of Billroth are cellular meshworks in the red pulp between the venous sinuses."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"63f35aa9a7c14e8cd5cd7d4874b1943173fc476cade805403440cbeb19c55f74","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-883cc9753bed":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Trabeculae","explanation":"Splenic trabeculae are connective-tissue extensions from the capsule that transmit vessels and provide structural support.","optionReasons":{"B":"Splenic trabeculae are connective-tissue extensions from the capsule that transmit vessels and provide structural support."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9300a7da58c8a38b47099af82d6b961553f79c48acfd1ea74e9d6af630d75f87","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-eec14fc551e1":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Outer cortex","explanation":"Outer or superficial cortex contains B-cell follicles; deep cortex, paracortex, tertiary and juxtamedullary cortex describe T-cell-rich cortical zones.","optionReasons":{"C":"Outer or superficial cortex contains B-cell follicles; deep cortex, paracortex, tertiary and juxtamedullary cortex describe T-cell-rich cortical zones."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4852290a47f2811c10d22eff75e967dc66d2550b226a6213dcb8f4b02c75c081","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-9601557cf015":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Hassall's corpuscles","explanation":"Hassall corpuscles are concentrically arranged, keratinizing epithelial reticular cells characteristic of the thymic medulla.","optionReasons":{"C":"Hassall corpuscles are concentrically arranged, keratinizing epithelial reticular cells characteristic of the thymic medulla."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"49b71b42e2eb52969837ebb6342e2b253d871e934e95a4571294bf15a386e206","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-98b9e9f21af3":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Peyer's patches","explanation":"Peyer patches are aggregated lymphoid follicles in the distal small intestine, especially the ileum.","optionReasons":{"C":"Peyer patches are aggregated lymphoid follicles in the distal small intestine, especially the ileum."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d41f8045922cd37d24b7bacf9ce4feb830af2354c87a05f3002e3044aa8a836c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-bbc545fc9845":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Central nervous system","explanation":"The healthy central nervous system lacks the conventional diffuse mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue present in gastrointestinal, genitourinary and respiratory mucosa.","optionReasons":{"B":"The healthy central nervous system lacks the conventional diffuse mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue present in gastrointestinal, genitourinary and respiratory mucosa."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e3e3be12bf7d1784be1694aac28a44e67e77b24fadb59ad342b4c9cc824bbf57","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-2b9c95d3b824":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Red pulp","explanation":"Splenic sinusoids are specialized venous channels in the red pulp, where circulating blood is filtered.","optionReasons":{"D":"Splenic sinusoids are specialized venous channels in the red pulp, where circulating blood is filtered."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f24e190d5e84820dc0c7761d613ee144a3d79139a0ad2dd1cd855c57db43fed1","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4ea36a37dd2a":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Periarterial lymphatic sheath","explanation":"PALS refers to the periarteriolar (also called periarterial) lymphoid sheath surrounding central arterioles, primarily composed of T lymphocytes.","optionReasons":{"C":"PALS refers to the periarteriolar (also called periarterial) lymphoid sheath surrounding central arterioles, primarily composed of T lymphocytes."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"cc808f9630f218a0364eb29d4b70759331ccd091af2dc5e35f611acaaf8a90e2","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-bd16f64ff4c8":{"correct":"C","answerText":"contains low concentration of myoglobin.","explanation":"Fast glycolytic muscle fibers have relatively little myoglobin, fewer mitochondria and lower capillary density than slow oxidative fibers.","optionReasons":{"C":"Fast glycolytic muscle fibers have relatively little myoglobin, fewer mitochondria and lower capillary density than slow oxidative fibers."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"76597c469db72fbffc3529b500c96bd1d9db567940776556d5a3c17e24c024c6","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-5cc2f15aa620":{"correct":"A","answerText":"voltage activated Na+ channels open.","explanation":"The initial upstroke of a normal nerve action potential follows opening of voltage-gated sodium channels and rapid inward sodium current.","optionReasons":{"A":"The initial upstroke of a normal nerve action potential follows opening of voltage-gated sodium channels and rapid inward sodium current."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"43dd64a3938d9b2f4da63ab78bbb5f1127f60e3754a4c1fbd7e55df1c9864dda","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-1fbdd3c25c12":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Diffusion of K+ ions outside the nerve fibers.","explanation":"Resting membrane potential depends heavily on potassium permeability and potassium diffusion down its concentration gradient, with ionic gradients maintained by Na+/K+-ATPase.","optionReasons":{"A":"Resting membrane potential depends heavily on potassium permeability and potassium diffusion down its concentration gradient, with ionic gradients maintained by Na+/K+-ATPase."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"39503466a8978fedd1dbdfce669234884c680026eb99f1fde122bb05b51a769e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-0f8f5af11257":{"correct":"B","answerText":"may reach up to 120 meter / second.","explanation":"Saltatory conduction occurs in myelinated axons and can be very fast, approaching 120 m/s in the largest peripheral fibers.","optionReasons":{"B":"Saltatory conduction occurs in myelinated axons and can be very fast, approaching 120 m/s in the largest peripheral fibers."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"51778b08b7189252a87af67aba7ba25cc27c836cd0a0ff452d545da0903db3a0","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-b813d6a6828e":{"correct":"D","answerText":"propagated without decrement. d","explanation":"Local graded potentials diminish with distance, may summate, and vary with stimulus strength; propagation without decrement characterizes action potentials.","optionReasons":{"D":"Local graded potentials diminish with distance, may summate, and vary with stimulus strength; propagation without decrement characterizes action potentials."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"64df7706df4b79514af1b1c4bed80b0a64068f85a67bec87f57fbda048ab7005","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-9fce28afae15":{"correct":"A","answerText":"A minimal stimulus produces a maximal response.","explanation":"A single excitable nerve fiber obeys the all-or-none principle: once threshold is reached an action potential is generated at essentially full amplitude.","optionReasons":{"A":"A single excitable nerve fiber obeys the all-or-none principle: once threshold is reached an action potential is generated at essentially full amplitude."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8ac55023291d9efbae44d88867428a74fc9a2af15558adccfe5c345838c710db","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-bc4fcd3529be":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Release of Ca++ from troponin.","explanation":"Excitation–contraction coupling involves release of calcium from sarcoplasmic reticulum and calcium binding to troponin, not release from troponin.","optionReasons":{"A":"Excitation–contraction coupling involves release of calcium from sarcoplasmic reticulum and calcium binding to troponin, not release from troponin."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"42e43adfa0e080c5b9acf37ccde650d9e526dc3f031ddc1b2b702c49bbbccd33","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a7d24abe4868":{"correct":"D","answerText":"C fibers. c","explanation":"Unmyelinated C fibers conduct more slowly than myelinated Aα, Aβ and B fibers due to small diameter and absent saltatory conduction.","optionReasons":{"D":"Unmyelinated C fibers conduct more slowly than myelinated Aα, Aβ and B fibers due to small diameter and absent saltatory conduction."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"caef0b06cb93a908489af8b9c0620843f3772496746bf3d95a2938507886da2e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e94ad9bb9ca6":{"correct":"C","answerText":"opening of Na+ and K+ channels at the same time.","explanation":"Acetylcholine opens nicotinic receptor channels at the motor end plate permeable to both sodium and potassium; net sodium influx generates depolarization.","optionReasons":{"C":"Acetylcholine opens nicotinic receptor channels at the motor end plate permeable to both sodium and potassium; net sodium influx generates depolarization."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"473d6e69e201363294ef98f2e24d1b3e33c3fb81c501e93496ae9d914c6bceae","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a7f441633984":{"correct":"D","answerText":"depends on anaerobic oxidation. d","explanation":"Slow oxidative red fibers depend on aerobic metabolism, not anaerobic oxidation; they are rich in mitochondria, myoglobin and capillaries.","optionReasons":{"D":"Slow oxidative red fibers depend on aerobic metabolism, not anaerobic oxidation; they are rich in mitochondria, myoglobin and capillaries."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ad7b2857fdc9550b056dfd10b8f129988a890d98dae530d702629578983f5a1f","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f6ec09ecad01":{"correct":"D","answerText":"succinylcholine. d","explanation":"Succinylcholine causes persistent nicotinic endplate depolarization followed by neuromuscular blockade; the other listed options tend to promote transmission.","optionReasons":{"D":"Succinylcholine causes persistent nicotinic endplate depolarization followed by neuromuscular blockade; the other listed options tend to promote transmission."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3d0baf7b93c6c918dd425c89be9323fdecc9fde4f4f28163c4faaea333de26aa","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-2926de390add":{"correct":"A","answerText":"is the distance between myosin and actin.","explanation":"A sarcomere extends from one Z disk to the next and shortens during contraction; it is not the distance between thick and thin filaments.","optionReasons":{"A":"A sarcomere extends from one Z disk to the next and shortens during contraction; it is not the distance between thick and thin filaments."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a9cb52928379d0f773ac3db9a22d96c96fa9134bc1b03ee66e1fd4fe0356af3e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a90ce120f353":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Metarteriole","explanation":"A metarteriole is a vascular channel connecting terminal arteriole to thoroughfare capillary bed, with intermittent smooth muscle cells.","optionReasons":{"D":"A metarteriole is a vascular channel connecting terminal arteriole to thoroughfare capillary bed, with intermittent smooth muscle cells."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1b6ef9f17aaa850c07114b68206ca09dc39067c57f0f100cde4aac3fb95bc86c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-44d5e8dac028":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Muscle","explanation":"The conventional portal vascular circuits are hepatic venous, renal arterial and hypothalamic–pituitary; ordinary skeletal muscle has no corresponding portal circuit.","optionReasons":{"C":"The conventional portal vascular circuits are hepatic venous, renal arterial and hypothalamic–pituitary; ordinary skeletal muscle has no corresponding portal circuit."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8abe303b28b5c512f162ffbabfb51c62a87dd0563278811831637a49840f562a","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-87669b9178ac":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Capillaries, arterioles, and post capillary venules","explanation":"The microvascular bed includes arterioles, capillary exchange vessels and postcapillary venules rather than larger conducting vessels.","optionReasons":{"C":"The microvascular bed includes arterioles, capillary exchange vessels and postcapillary venules rather than larger conducting vessels."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e9fb60da2f1043c534028842c006e63519fcad040c17440f55219624af93a1b9","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ef07d6b8bc44":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Sinusoidal capillaries","explanation":"Sinusoidal capillaries have wide lumens and discontinuous endothelial gaps, making them particularly permeable.","optionReasons":{"C":"Sinusoidal capillaries have wide lumens and discontinuous endothelial gaps, making them particularly permeable."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e2d1e6c9b47991fa517b789e612914dc68059738905fe7ef0518af5374fc2156","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-933856d81e24":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Kidney","explanation":"The glomerular capillary tuft is interposed between afferent and efferent arterioles in the renal arterial portal circulation.","optionReasons":{"A":"The glomerular capillary tuft is interposed between afferent and efferent arterioles in the renal arterial portal circulation."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d7e7b4d12b5a0a27aa88fa0ec0b2ad900c5f69b531fcdedf6695e85f9c8ae890","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-80b39d21ffb3":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Blood vessels","explanation":"Vasa vasorum are small blood vessels that provide nourishment to the outer walls of large blood vessels.","optionReasons":{"E":"Vasa vasorum are small blood vessels that provide nourishment to the outer walls of large blood vessels."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"79d7852fcbdb94cf5d123597d24e2dee0fb66deb67f194d0ff28b29e4ea003d5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-04701e3cb394":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Elastic artery","explanation":"The aorta is an elastic conducting artery with many elastic lamellae in its tunica media.","optionReasons":{"D":"The aorta is an elastic conducting artery with many elastic lamellae in its tunica media."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8b08cf95f024af4b599cee760130552b9b5d5222f53589b7471e535950920260","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-8a878f837310":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Fenestrated capillaries","explanation":"Fenestrated capillaries are defined by endothelial pores that permit relatively rapid molecular exchange.","optionReasons":{"B":"Fenestrated capillaries are defined by endothelial pores that permit relatively rapid molecular exchange."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6d2c7b91f2f4b17730412fcee525dda0d0138ad25d70969e3d28d8185f19cbc3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7c57f69cecd7":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Pericyte","explanation":"Pericytes surround capillaries and postcapillary venules and can help regulate vessel stability and repair; they retain differentiation potential.","optionReasons":{"C":"Pericytes surround capillaries and postcapillary venules and can help regulate vessel stability and repair; they retain differentiation potential."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ebb8649c37261f17af616600a8fb704e8dbab7d134dcb28653d5cd0123d6c5b8","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-2fef7b85962b":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Nerves","explanation":"Nervi vasorum denotes the autonomic nerves supplying blood vessel walls and regulating smooth-muscle tone.","optionReasons":{"D":"Nervi vasorum denotes the autonomic nerves supplying blood vessel walls and regulating smooth-muscle tone."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"00bb9bad0a46dc22e14044d2861060f4d60412cc0181a89cc4efb9772e45b55c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-3d8067e41dc6":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Venule","explanation":"Venules receive blood from the capillary plexus and drain into progressively larger veins.","optionReasons":{"C":"Venules receive blood from the capillary plexus and drain into progressively larger veins."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b3ac511228eb931e72615e1ee463c19a9e23d721aa40c814332ecf90731ae8cc","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c8de687b442c":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Venous sinus","explanation":"The dural venous sinuses form the intracranial venous channels that drain cerebral and meningeal veins.","optionReasons":{"E":"The dural venous sinuses form the intracranial venous channels that drain cerebral and meningeal veins."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b3678020d7ec4b31de255c5e98196e7669ee245509599355fb173d2c0c36a7c3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-472aa2c1e80b":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Thymus","explanation":"The thymic stromal framework is made chiefly by epithelial reticular cells, unlike the reticular-fiber frameworks of lymph nodes, spleen and marrow.","optionReasons":{"D":"The thymic stromal framework is made chiefly by epithelial reticular cells, unlike the reticular-fiber frameworks of lymph nodes, spleen and marrow."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7db34a6c3790464f751aa9e2e86e2e446caa8a740c5818696f087cb09a6e35ad","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-57ce106b362f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"GALT","explanation":"GALT means gut-associated lymphoid tissue, part of mucosal immune defenses.","optionReasons":{"D":"GALT means gut-associated lymphoid tissue, part of mucosal immune defenses."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bd4806415ccf1ebb8fd7fbbe2600d0ba6c9d881ba7d6385e13242d603fc3a525","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-b557a8e82ebf":{"correct":"E","answerText":"All of the above are functions of the spleen","explanation":"Splenic functions include red-cell clearance, adaptive immune responses, blood reservoir function and hematopoiesis during fetal development.","optionReasons":{"E":"Splenic functions include red-cell clearance, adaptive immune responses, blood reservoir function and hematopoiesis during fetal development."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1c940a6dcbc8ded90f4087cfdb91fc8b0fca5c1a750c1d3e996ccf64bf4497d0","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e92390811a3c":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Outer cortex","explanation":"Lymphatic nodules/follicles are located chiefly in the B-cell-rich outer cortex, unlike T-cell-rich paracortex.","optionReasons":{"E":"Lymphatic nodules/follicles are located chiefly in the B-cell-rich outer cortex, unlike T-cell-rich paracortex."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"10f4e964b27265a8518e1dc53d7cf88bbe39fc0cf501787b41b146442f0a0ad3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-748c140ead11":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Germinal center","explanation":"Secondary follicles contain germinal centers with activated, proliferating B cells undergoing affinity maturation.","optionReasons":{"A":"Secondary follicles contain germinal centers with activated, proliferating B cells undergoing affinity maturation."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"30660e0a78c1f745a3f5721cefe8186dd78eac14bd1ca7febf502c1e28a7629f","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c6ad6d225f2c":{"correct":"A","answerText":"BALT","explanation":"BALT denotes bronchus-associated lymphoid tissue in the airway mucosa.","optionReasons":{"A":"BALT denotes bronchus-associated lymphoid tissue in the airway mucosa."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e502a297abd3f8b7a3b5985ed22dc79305f0c16f360e024abfba328fdf5ef38b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-46d8e5375260":{"correct":"B","answerText":"White pulp","explanation":"Splenic white pulp is the organized lymphocyte-rich tissue surrounding central arteries and follicles.","optionReasons":{"B":"Splenic white pulp is the organized lymphocyte-rich tissue surrounding central arteries and follicles."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c7e810839c71c8b8828b7fcbb8424f3f8b318d3bab1c6894d3673e83bcfa2c25","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-649776c547a9":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Cords of Billroth","explanation":"Billroth cords are red-pulp tissue between sinusoidal channels in the spleen.","optionReasons":{"A":"Billroth cords are red-pulp tissue between sinusoidal channels in the spleen."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d835c72dba6e6ec7cb3f0111e9b611bf413df1b09db65ddab7f903520faf5afa","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4e5aec62d7ec":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Trabeculae","explanation":"Trabeculae are extensions of splenic connective tissue capsule projecting into the parenchyma.","optionReasons":{"B":"Trabeculae are extensions of splenic connective tissue capsule projecting into the parenchyma."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9300a7da58c8a38b47099af82d6b961553f79c48acfd1ea74e9d6af630d75f87","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-5375d454d66f":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Outer cortex","explanation":"Outer cortex is the lymph-node follicular zone; the other terms describe deep cortex/paracortex.","optionReasons":{"C":"Outer cortex is the lymph-node follicular zone; the other terms describe deep cortex/paracortex."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a44c4009648a4fa317a879b75bfaddcd3ed3d84e5262a824c4fa17c0c29251b5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-df6a48496065":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Hassall's corpuscles","explanation":"The thymic medulla contains Hassall corpuscles formed from concentrically arranged epithelial reticular cells.","optionReasons":{"C":"The thymic medulla contains Hassall corpuscles formed from concentrically arranged epithelial reticular cells."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3c9dcf21112c7051be162fa88b2bf78018e9741e0382ae6533b10830ce799652","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-79400033bd97":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Peyer's patches","explanation":"Aggregated lymphoid follicles in the ileum are called Peyer patches.","optionReasons":{"C":"Aggregated lymphoid follicles in the ileum are called Peyer patches."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d41f8045922cd37d24b7bacf9ce4feb830af2354c87a05f3002e3044aa8a836c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7479af1b34ab":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Central nervous system","explanation":"Conventional diffuse mucosal lymphoid tissue is absent from healthy CNS tissue but present in GI, GU and respiratory systems.","optionReasons":{"B":"Conventional diffuse mucosal lymphoid tissue is absent from healthy CNS tissue but present in GI, GU and respiratory systems."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"23615b44f01c280badc86b5acb3bbf7a31ee4ff3f73740654841a22fa38aa571","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f2b567c6c57a":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Red pulp","explanation":"Splenic venous sinuses occur within the red pulp and permit selective filtration of blood cells.","optionReasons":{"D":"Splenic venous sinuses occur within the red pulp and permit selective filtration of blood cells."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f24e190d5e84820dc0c7761d613ee144a3d79139a0ad2dd1cd855c57db43fed1","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-5c61a2149c7f":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Periarterial lymphatic sheath","explanation":"PALS means periarteriolar lymphoid sheath, the T-lymphocyte region around splenic central arterioles.","optionReasons":{"C":"PALS means periarteriolar lymphoid sheath, the T-lymphocyte region around splenic central arterioles."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dd36461522869845070ccf51b797ddf0d7129388ca16fcb1af86dcbb743b0c4d","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-8c7e58664674":{"correct":"E","answerText":"It passes to the abdomen at the level of T12","explanation":"The descending thoracic aorta traverses the aortic hiatus at the T12 vertebral level to become the abdominal aorta.","optionReasons":{"E":"The descending thoracic aorta traverses the aortic hiatus at the T12 vertebral level to become the abdominal aorta."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fea36e88868d96fa8bdc740e386601399ce432aaa353326da83f740e3c771299","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-b1b360c44454":{"correct":"E","answerText":"The apex of the lung is above the thoracic inlet","explanation":"The lung apex extends into the root of the neck above the superior thoracic aperture, covered by cervical pleura.","optionReasons":{"E":"The lung apex extends into the root of the neck above the superior thoracic aperture, covered by cervical pleura."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6b46f2179a52de76c980060181c5c6c4d1795818487b4a680badfa7d451e4269","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c7768e8a5a6e":{"correct":"D","answerText":"10th","explanation":"Parietal pleura typically reflects inferiorly to the 8th rib at the midclavicular line, 10th at the midaxillary line and 12th posteriorly.","optionReasons":{"D":"Parietal pleura typically reflects inferiorly to the 8th rib at the midclavicular line, 10th at the midaxillary line and 12th posteriorly."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"afab9f62a9cd2dd7b7f357d26dade6a89b8439fd96a34ba22daf200472185fb0","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-889ab6c89442":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Anterior descending","explanation":"Anterior interventricular (left anterior descending) coronary artery supplies the anterior two-thirds of the interventricular septum via septal perforators.","optionReasons":{"D":"Anterior interventricular (left anterior descending) coronary artery supplies the anterior two-thirds of the interventricular septum via septal perforators."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0c18334a04451f5d41cdcc1845ee449ec6b55abfcbdc495ff0e1dee9d3544e06","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-338c403293d1":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Right supplies the posterior descending branch in most patients","explanation":"Right coronary artery gives rise to the posterior interventricular artery in right-dominant circulation, the majority of people.","optionReasons":{"C":"Right coronary artery gives rise to the posterior interventricular artery in right-dominant circulation, the majority of people."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"542d566a9361bff71f0e1f25cad3940909c3859b4eae624ba12dbd81329e9121","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-90ddb5156dac":{"correct":"B","answerText":"anterior cardiac vein","explanation":"Anterior cardiac veins generally drain directly into the right atrium rather than through the coronary sinus.","optionReasons":{"B":"Anterior cardiac veins generally drain directly into the right atrium rather than through the coronary sinus."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"394e2ac85759ae8d19253a0a96fe2258e42c90bddeae1b14f51d72e3a1f9f775","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-de179331c637":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Mitral incompetence","explanation":"A pansystolic murmur is characteristic of mitral regurgitation because a left ventricle–left atrium pressure gradient persists throughout systole.","optionReasons":{"A":"A pansystolic murmur is characteristic of mitral regurgitation because a left ventricle–left atrium pressure gradient persists throughout systole."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bd14896875931695d96aa6a3ec6154e0a40b79fb5ef00c05834bc1c143e7c91c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-131046ad5392":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Left ventricular hypertrophy","explanation":"A sustained, laterally displaced apex beat suggests left ventricular hypertrophy; marked displacement also raises concern for LV enlargement.","optionReasons":{"C":"A sustained, laterally displaced apex beat suggests left ventricular hypertrophy; marked displacement also raises concern for LV enlargement."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a189f49a5a0c463b8a5e82c5aae4d7aff2b568ff7dfc98b02fb1af89c4b238c3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-2baebd8590ba":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Mitral stenosis","explanation":"A palpable low-pitched diastolic thrill at the cardiac apex suggests significant mitral stenosis due to turbulent diastolic inflow.","optionReasons":{"D":"A palpable low-pitched diastolic thrill at the cardiac apex suggests significant mitral stenosis due to turbulent diastolic inflow."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7acf670e221a67b9c8ec279d65a484d27a9f0d769cd360344fad73202941673f","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-86eff2444641":{"correct":"D","answerText":"The pulse is irregularly irregular","explanation":"Atrial fibrillation causes irregularly irregular ventricular activation and an irregular peripheral pulse, often with a pulse deficit.","optionReasons":{"D":"Atrial fibrillation causes irregularly irregular ventricular activation and an irregular peripheral pulse, often with a pulse deficit."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6c675d2ed130adb4a2597ae7560d985877777166c29a44e6f7de7ac05fca8aaf","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-44b9d0dab2d9":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Pulmonary oedema without pleural effusions","explanation":"Bronchial breath sounds, tracheal deviation from volume loss and supra/infraclavicular recession can all occur with advanced upper-lobe tuberculosis.","optionReasons":{"D":"Bronchial breath sounds, tracheal deviation from volume loss and supra/infraclavicular recession can all occur with advanced upper-lobe tuberculosis."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1a946b8da9f7353f6eaf5e7ef2251913ee1e62f53a5a9e8e097b1e7f36d07cde","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7fbc0bb7d5d2":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Abdominal distension can result from ascites, marked splenic enlargement and ovarian masses; all the listed mechanisms are possible.","optionReasons":{"D":"Abdominal distension can result from ascites, marked splenic enlargement and ovarian masses; all the listed mechanisms are possible."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e15b7946b4c7d82f1ccc7d53e603cb725f88b72c53d1a47d40a1f445479a9ae4","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-eb77aed78d5b":{"correct":"C","answerText":"By demonstrating shifting dullness to be present","explanation":"Shifting dullness is a physical-examination maneuver for detecting free intraperitoneal fluid; unlike tenderness, it reflects fluid movement with position.","optionReasons":{"C":"Shifting dullness is a physical-examination maneuver for detecting free intraperitoneal fluid; unlike tenderness, it reflects fluid movement with position."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"77d8b922aaa0ea11b77f0e68a516566ab50d77f839523de7805c59764c9fd7f0","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-1157a870a658":{"correct":"B","answerText":"May be caused by acute expansion of an abdominal aortic aneurysm","explanation":"Expansion or rupture of an abdominal aortic aneurysm can cause an acute abdomen and is a time-critical emergency.","optionReasons":{"B":"Expansion or rupture of an abdominal aortic aneurysm can cause an acute abdomen and is a time-critical emergency."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"08549d404c08ad85c4095ea2c35d530a69eeaacfceedba428b28ac2e07e4bd45","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-56d22aabc4dd":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Indicates inflammation of the parietal peritoneum at the site of tenderness","explanation":"Rebound tenderness is pain on sudden release of pressure due to irritation of inflamed parietal peritoneum; it is not specific for one diagnosis.","optionReasons":{"C":"Rebound tenderness is pain on sudden release of pressure due to irritation of inflamed parietal peritoneum; it is not specific for one diagnosis."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4703efad8429e801c20d925881511916d13394f39579f4cc3a903c1ce441dbcd","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-d938f12d5af2":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Suggests bilateral XII palsy of a lower motor neuron type","explanation":"Bilateral tongue atrophy and fasciculations indicate a lower-motor-neuron process affecting hypoglossal nuclei or their axons.","optionReasons":{"A":"Bilateral tongue atrophy and fasciculations indicate a lower-motor-neuron process affecting hypoglossal nuclei or their axons."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5373ff99922ac5b629dccb3959d2fa0612f0823b3b67a6e7635e1380d37d49b6","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c0833e61e1a4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"May be present in a transverse myelitis","explanation":"An extensor plantar response is an upper motor neuron/corticospinal tract sign and may occur with transverse myelitis.","optionReasons":{"B":"An extensor plantar response is an upper motor neuron/corticospinal tract sign and may occur with transverse myelitis."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"2951318d22fd393eeb569c122fecbfc77de0a008d310d7253a44076cafa9c2b3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-8c4f3292b4c7":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Idiosyncrasy","explanation":"An idiosyncratic drug reaction is an uncommon, unpredictable response that may reflect individual susceptibility rather than the usual dose-dependent pharmacology.","optionReasons":{"A":"An idiosyncratic drug reaction is an uncommon, unpredictable response that may reflect individual susceptibility rather than the usual dose-dependent pharmacology."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"823e750ded243b4fab6c5b76c43271c65109f6981f0829904d5f407952138108","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ed31ddfa2f8f":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Atropine","explanation":"Atropine is a muscarinic antagonist that relaxes smooth muscle; older pharmacology questions include relief of smooth-muscle spasm among its uses.","optionReasons":{"C":"Atropine is a muscarinic antagonist that relaxes smooth muscle; older pharmacology questions include relief of smooth-muscle spasm among its uses."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7c48c84166794369d678c752d516f9a4fb22254722378ca70da35b3cf8efdb83","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f80856c3e053":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Rapacuronium","explanation":"Rapacuronium was an unusually rapid-onset nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocker, although it was withdrawn because of severe bronchospasm risk.","optionReasons":{"B":"Rapacuronium was an unusually rapid-onset nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocker, although it was withdrawn because of severe bronchospasm risk."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f3fca386cb891154104625f235c40562ccb4bbc411ec74582c73a4c1f229444b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-fc9daa9ecfb9":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Phentolamine","explanation":"Phentolamine is a competitive nonselective alpha-adrenergic antagonist used for local catecholamine-extravasation vasoconstriction.","optionReasons":{"B":"Phentolamine is a competitive nonselective alpha-adrenergic antagonist used for local catecholamine-extravasation vasoconstriction."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e15ac5c348fda7273a31839b3fb24bfe24ad536523eaf8c483c02a1d806ecac3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ce20e159e848":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Sotalol","explanation":"Sotalol blocks beta receptors without clinically relevant intrinsic sympathomimetic or membrane-stabilizing activity; it also has class III potassium-channel blockade.","optionReasons":{"C":"Sotalol blocks beta receptors without clinically relevant intrinsic sympathomimetic or membrane-stabilizing activity; it also has class III potassium-channel blockade."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"696e56571105766dd811be79687bd7c839f8079db6d5cc8fc33388d16a79c605","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4a4e19cfa932":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Valproate acts by several mechanisms, including voltage-gated sodium-channel effects, modulation of T-type calcium currents, and increased inhibitory GABA activity.","optionReasons":{"D":"Valproate acts by several mechanisms, including voltage-gated sodium-channel effects, modulation of T-type calcium currents, and increased inhibitory GABA activity."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"29d8a63a9c3429e9c61ab4b716785661becd57f869d25da924c4aa28870d4e58","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-651ec2a9ab65":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Trihexyphenidyl","explanation":"Trihexyphenidyl is a centrally acting antimuscarinic agent used for selected Parkinson tremor and medication-induced extrapyramidal symptoms.","optionReasons":{"C":"Trihexyphenidyl is a centrally acting antimuscarinic agent used for selected Parkinson tremor and medication-induced extrapyramidal symptoms."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5aa8f7c179a85f1554591eeb015192006bfc824a84658a60aa5e301b0e4bbf7c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ba52148ec6cb":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Tramadol","explanation":"Tramadol combines relatively weak mu-opioid receptor agonism with inhibition of norepinephrine and serotonin reuptake, accounting for mixed opioid and nonopioid mechanisms.","optionReasons":{"B":"Tramadol combines relatively weak mu-opioid receptor agonism with inhibition of norepinephrine and serotonin reuptake, accounting for mixed opioid and nonopioid mechanisms."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0d4d6312f849bd360e6722a7d9f344b16acd4330ffe55ded5eab83190dc500b7","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-fe648d10e9ea":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Psychosis","explanation":"Antipsychotic (neuroleptic) agents mainly treat psychotic symptoms such as hallucinations and delusions; they are not standard primary therapy for the other listed conditions.","optionReasons":{"B":"Antipsychotic (neuroleptic) agents mainly treat psychotic symptoms such as hallucinations and delusions; they are not standard primary therapy for the other listed conditions."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"062915ff490e7299749888ae1482af99acb712809443d9e19afca588d684c52d","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-edb700acf05f":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Strongly block postsynaptic d2receptor","explanation":"Many conventional antipsychotics block postsynaptic dopamine D2 receptors, reducing mesolimbic dopaminergic signaling.","optionReasons":{"A":"Many conventional antipsychotics block postsynaptic dopamine D2 receptors, reducing mesolimbic dopaminergic signaling."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f14da80785a1f89fcb0686432277157e4e0192b1b22c30134a7e99ea202a510d","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-9ad88a3d19d1":{"correct":"C","answerText":"The mesolimbic and mesofrontal systems","explanation":"Mesolimbic and mesocortical (mesofrontal) dopamine circuits are heavily involved in motivation, reward and behavioral regulation.","optionReasons":{"C":"Mesolimbic and mesocortical (mesofrontal) dopamine circuits are heavily involved in motivation, reward and behavioral regulation."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4ccfb11e5179b439a6dcc0aadb6c08c3d5bba036884328b8c3be32c80b8524e3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f38b617771c9":{"correct":"B","answerText":"The pituitary","explanation":"Dopamine tonically inhibits prolactin secretion from anterior-pituitary lactotrophs, so D2 antagonism at the pituitary elevates prolactin.","optionReasons":{"B":"Dopamine tonically inhibits prolactin secretion from anterior-pituitary lactotrophs, so D2 antagonism at the pituitary elevates prolactin."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"63df609ea3a39d3fc7fb1ce851d000088750645fbdfe50adbf47ae96957a391c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f6bfd63bf6aa":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Benztropine mesylate","explanation":"Benztropine can treat acute dystonia and some drug-induced parkinsonian extrapyramidal symptoms via antimuscarinic action; tardive dyskinesia requires a different approach.","optionReasons":{"B":"Benztropine can treat acute dystonia and some drug-induced parkinsonian extrapyramidal symptoms via antimuscarinic action; tardive dyskinesia requires a different approach."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c00c64c0e0f08469dfc48e9085a264b8d964ecbe420ec0d57e99641ccbe99c18","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-9539ef96af8b":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Haloperidol","explanation":"Haloperidol is a first-generation or typical antipsychotic with potent D2-receptor antagonism.","optionReasons":{"C":"Haloperidol is a first-generation or typical antipsychotic with potent D2-receptor antagonism."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9e9c269f279ebdd58ebe1cf06ef14267de3849a8281d208fa1e1c6ca88cc30b9","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-d342673468a2":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Clozapine","explanation":"Clozapine is a second-generation atypical antipsychotic distinguished by low extrapyramidal adverse effects but serious hematologic and metabolic risks.","optionReasons":{"B":"Clozapine is a second-generation atypical antipsychotic distinguished by low extrapyramidal adverse effects but serious hematologic and metabolic risks."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"cd3c694e57ca8215ff64bd55efd825912ae2f2858030c994953a1445465a73e3","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ca7dfc28790e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Hyperactive dopaminergic state in the presence of dopamine blockers","explanation":"Tardive dyskinesia is associated with dopamine-receptor supersensitivity and maladaptive basal-ganglia signaling after prolonged receptor blockade.","optionReasons":{"B":"Tardive dyskinesia is associated with dopamine-receptor supersensitivity and maladaptive basal-ganglia signaling after prolonged receptor blockade."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d1839f980225f018298d2e39c6e1aaf73d3a7b42036cdeee40a226e834b8f987","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c0536f73dffd":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Clozapine","explanation":"Clozapine interacts with multiple receptors including D4 and serotonin 5-HT2 receptors and has relatively low striatal D2 occupancy.","optionReasons":{"A":"Clozapine interacts with multiple receptors including D4 and serotonin 5-HT2 receptors and has relatively low striatal D2 occupancy."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"783c0e7fb0d685c8ac4dad206413390df690ef4237c018a00fb739c7d1b73dfd","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-1af11d4b4fef":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Chlorpromazine","explanation":"Chlorpromazine is a low-potency aliphatic phenothiazine first-generation antipsychotic.","optionReasons":{"C":"Chlorpromazine is a low-potency aliphatic phenothiazine first-generation antipsychotic."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c73a64dac7efb767dbc8b85c45af84569f8c268caf02289c9cd484512fe655fb","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-887c2d32ef64":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Thiothixene","explanation":"Thiothixene is a thioxanthene-class conventional antipsychotic, whereas chlorpromazine is a phenothiazine.","optionReasons":{"D":"Thiothixene is a thioxanthene-class conventional antipsychotic, whereas chlorpromazine is a phenothiazine."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7dc34a170050e739bbdcb91f15bb8da94f5ff8d376b11c2c6d55e3a9044c599f","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a478e90e4289":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Clozapine","explanation":"Clozapine belongs to the dibenzodiazepine chemical family and has broad dopamine, serotonin, muscarinic and histamine-receptor interactions.","optionReasons":{"B":"Clozapine belongs to the dibenzodiazepine chemical family and has broad dopamine, serotonin, muscarinic and histamine-receptor interactions."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7112d89ca10b7f5f856441c4aabaa1b6b7a73e0cf65d552d8b6a2fed822b14e5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f4733c0eddc7":{"correct":"A","answerText":"In the chemoreceptor trigger zone of the medulla","explanation":"Phenothiazine antipsychotics reduce emesis by blocking D2 receptors in the chemoreceptor trigger zone of the area postrema.","optionReasons":{"A":"Phenothiazine antipsychotics reduce emesis by blocking D2 receptors in the chemoreceptor trigger zone of the area postrema."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6e13ce523d6cb8be4e127f9f018ea067c89800c9477b2ac533fb80c3f98d90be","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-57c54c0f6977":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Alter temperature-regulating mechanisms producing hypothermia","explanation":"Phenothiazines can disrupt thermoregulatory mechanisms and produce hypothermia, particularly with sedating, low-potency drugs.","optionReasons":{"A":"Phenothiazines can disrupt thermoregulatory mechanisms and produce hypothermia, particularly with sedating, low-potency drugs."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5333ea87f791e35936a06da39d13da4c97166e00c5479b363065a0035278d39f","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-25edcf5c74e5":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Many phenothiazines have dopaminergic, muscarinic and H1-histamine receptor antagonism, producing therapeutic and adverse effects.","optionReasons":{"D":"Many phenothiazines have dopaminergic, muscarinic and H1-histamine receptor antagonism, producing therapeutic and adverse effects."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"571afbe9ecd170fb5b242cbf9a7973f886c81e76378588bf978855826e8cb736","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-fa3d2d242b7c":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Clozapine, chlorpromazine and olanzapine all antagonize H1-histamine receptors, contributing to sedation and weight gain.","optionReasons":{"D":"Clozapine, chlorpromazine and olanzapine all antagonize H1-histamine receptors, contributing to sedation and weight gain."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5ff91224204698de4e45e76d3fbaf137ad19069e06840ee2984c0bf232a91dd5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-be30de14de92":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Alpha adrenoreceptor blockade","explanation":"Alpha-1-adrenoceptor blockade decreases vasoconstrictor tone when standing and may cause orthostatic hypotension.","optionReasons":{"C":"Alpha-1-adrenoceptor blockade decreases vasoconstrictor tone when standing and may cause orthostatic hypotension."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1e1a22be1e1d67022840d758fe9d808da0b5b0ca54838753ba80a31f542aded2","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-534dd90a6cb4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Muscarinic cholinoreceptor blockade","explanation":"Dry mouth, urinary retention, blurred near vision, constipation and tachycardia arise from muscarinic receptor blockade.","optionReasons":{"B":"Dry mouth, urinary retention, blurred near vision, constipation and tachycardia arise from muscarinic receptor blockade."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a6abe63375cb7efd126aa7891dd990d99d8668a88929875245305d968d1d76de","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-d03993646235":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Blocking D2 receptors","explanation":"Haloperidol is a potent antagonist of dopamine D2 receptors, its main mechanism for antipsychotic efficacy.","optionReasons":{"A":"Haloperidol is a potent antagonist of dopamine D2 receptors, its main mechanism for antipsychotic efficacy."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b44f9ead98b32c6feec84efd12a0b6130c8a290556e2930550bb37819bd9f15e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-d09869d2d454":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Has potent anticholinergic activity","explanation":"Clozapine has significant antimuscarinic activity and is also associated with constipation, sedation, metabolic dysfunction and agranulocytosis.","optionReasons":{"A":"Clozapine has significant antimuscarinic activity and is also associated with constipation, sedation, metabolic dysfunction and agranulocytosis."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c2a5ff3ae82869cd81f2a8e4fcc57d1742410ec1c2884cfe7ccd543348c5ff59","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-57f396f186a1":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Clozapine","explanation":"Clozapine may cause severe neutropenia/agranulocytosis and lowers seizure threshold, necessitating blood-count monitoring under applicable regulations.","optionReasons":{"C":"Clozapine may cause severe neutropenia/agranulocytosis and lowers seizure threshold, necessitating blood-count monitoring under applicable regulations."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"794169c90fe0d5cb66d637d304a294363b4f1a16df60901782529f7b51931a24","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-83dc289feef0":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Risperidone","explanation":"Risperidone antagonizes both D2-dopamine and 5-HT2-serotonin receptors, a characteristic atypical antipsychotic profile.","optionReasons":{"D":"Risperidone antagonizes both D2-dopamine and 5-HT2-serotonin receptors, a characteristic atypical antipsychotic profile."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5bc89b29accbef805feb363c58921f947ffd645956c4bdb13038154ee240e8f4","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-77b1095d1f05":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Bipolar disorder","explanation":"Lithium is a classic mood stabilizer used particularly for treatment and relapse prevention in bipolar disorder.","optionReasons":{"B":"Lithium is a classic mood stabilizer used particularly for treatment and relapse prevention in bipolar disorder."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f2c8030a973accca0079862140aaea571a0f6ead32fbd72b37ff1257f5044089","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-3183cc27f39b":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Lithium affects intracellular second-messenger pathways, neurotransmission and cation-related signaling; no single mechanism fully accounts for its therapeutic actions.","optionReasons":{"D":"Lithium affects intracellular second-messenger pathways, neurotransmission and cation-related signaling; no single mechanism fully accounts for its therapeutic actions."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bc83664ebd2c4e0ee0082259160fb11ed50ace62d396be0ff57138ad7a79083f","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-fb9cdaee73f4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Decrease catecholamine-related activity","explanation":"Lithium has complex actions but can reduce catecholamine-related signaling, contributing to mood stabilization.","optionReasons":{"B":"Lithium has complex actions but can reduce catecholamine-related signaling, contributing to mood stabilization."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0bd77c340f818ad95ddabe96f10ab11f751908c4ddb22ee56da90ce9d062fa58","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-46d837b5c269":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above PART VIII Antidepressant agents","explanation":"Lithium may cause goiter/hypothyroidism and nephrogenic diabetes insipidus; fetal cardiac risk is increased with exposure early in pregnancy.","optionReasons":{"D":"Lithium may cause goiter/hypothyroidism and nephrogenic diabetes insipidus; fetal cardiac risk is increased with exposure early in pregnancy."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6afbab1c1c5bd38e6da0b3f002d88b3c7033db1ec137ccd0956acb396b6ed857","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-b0c9058247cb":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Amitriptyline","explanation":"Amitriptyline is a tricyclic antidepressant that inhibits serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake and also blocks several other receptor classes.","optionReasons":{"B":"Amitriptyline is a tricyclic antidepressant that inhibits serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake and also blocks several other receptor classes."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bb7421c847e4d8b69164a43f5fe3993d9d726583e3993ee7664c46f2d0d37dae","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-c9a09479091d":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Maprotiline","explanation":"Maprotiline is a tetracyclic second-generation antidepressant with prominent norepinephrine-reuptake inhibition.","optionReasons":{"A":"Maprotiline is a tetracyclic second-generation antidepressant with prominent norepinephrine-reuptake inhibition."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e1bf815e1261c1c1d11d49eb3d397477d04775550d7769b39e7fe56f1342599d","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7733b9752b66":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Fluoxetine","explanation":"Fluoxetine is an SSRI that selectively blocks the serotonin transporter and increases synaptic 5-HT.","optionReasons":{"D":"Fluoxetine is an SSRI that selectively blocks the serotonin transporter and increases synaptic 5-HT."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"24ccf38b590861c92c9a1ad948f94aa97c9442332fa0d9ff6a5315ab85509945","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-493a01a96df9":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Maprotiline","explanation":"Maprotiline is a predominantly noradrenergic reuptake inhibitor; fluvoxamine is serotonergic and tranylcypromine inhibits monoamine oxidase.","optionReasons":{"B":"Maprotiline is a predominantly noradrenergic reuptake inhibitor; fluvoxamine is serotonergic and tranylcypromine inhibits monoamine oxidase."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"44ce6ef94bcd382ce9c66e462a7c0377f909791748273f1ca723d4a79124c9d0","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4ec2bbf8a0bf":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Amitriptyline","explanation":"Amitriptyline blocks reuptake of both norepinephrine and serotonin through NET and SERT inhibition.","optionReasons":{"A":"Amitriptyline blocks reuptake of both norepinephrine and serotonin through NET and SERT inhibition."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"12b00e1d6cd125f90cf130751b4b87e3b32e6c3089530d259f7d224eb84a0cee","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4e59be04c060":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Phenelzine","explanation":"Phenelzine is a hydrazine-derived, irreversible nonselective monoamine-oxidase inhibitor.","optionReasons":{"D":"Phenelzine is a hydrazine-derived, irreversible nonselective monoamine-oxidase inhibitor."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4a4a802b2aecd0f05a4b90994b8279ae8aa26df4e17f7fec38760862e726718e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-ffe373e3fe55":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Tranylcypramine","explanation":"Tranylcypromine is an irreversible, nonhydrazine MAOI structurally related to amphetamine.","optionReasons":{"C":"Tranylcypromine is an irreversible, nonhydrazine MAOI structurally related to amphetamine."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"21e4237fae18179468f240b85c6b1861eae621fbef04c25e3a7ad79b951638cc","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-a83402dcb130":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Moclobemide","explanation":"Moclobemide is a reversible, selective monoamine oxidase A inhibitor with a shorter pharmacodynamic action than irreversible MAO inhibitors.","optionReasons":{"C":"Moclobemide is a reversible, selective monoamine oxidase A inhibitor with a shorter pharmacodynamic action than irreversible MAO inhibitors."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"cf69f5a027f0e53ffbedcdf2ec67394bbc36e3141f7288459baf987017550c5c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-5961c3e664f8":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Is responsible for norepinephrine, serotonin, and tyramine metabolism","explanation":"MAO-A preferentially metabolizes serotonin, norepinephrine and tyramine, whereas MAO-B preferentially acts on substrates such as phenethylamine.","optionReasons":{"A":"MAO-A preferentially metabolizes serotonin, norepinephrine and tyramine, whereas MAO-B preferentially acts on substrates such as phenethylamine."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fb99052079f9d171e8a940bc5472768d1021bb734ecc68eb70294b22c5d247da","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-4fa447d848c6":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Blocking a major degradative pathway for the amine neurotransmitters, which permits more amines to accumulate in presynaptic stores","explanation":"MAO inhibitors block intracellular oxidative deamination of monoamine neurotransmitters, increasing amine availability.","optionReasons":{"B":"MAO inhibitors block intracellular oxidative deamination of monoamine neurotransmitters, increasing amine availability."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"88b2abfefddabc8c9d8e14c50ac83f394cee16d84bb8d5ac1da0e83e3b691ab6","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f172e3652dd5":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Hypertensive reactions to tyramine ingested in food","explanation":"Irreversible MAO inhibition prevents tyramine metabolism and can precipitate severe hypertensive reactions after tyramine-rich foods.","optionReasons":{"C":"Irreversible MAO inhibition prevents tyramine metabolism and can precipitate severe hypertensive reactions after tyramine-rich foods."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f604a672964aac62d64aa4f46a68c4d34044d6116c6d363c5bccd715bdcc6e34","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-57822a9f0bfa":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Combining MAO inhibitors with SSRIs, many tricyclics or sympathomimetics can trigger serious serotonin toxicity or hypertensive crises.","optionReasons":{"D":"Combining MAO inhibitors with SSRIs, many tricyclics or sympathomimetics can trigger serious serotonin toxicity or hypertensive crises."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"deeaa3c9ca317ef1ed51cd9292bd69e9f2d4f35fca6ce7fbbc2ffb94dfa6175e","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-06f470492473":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Significant accumulation of amine neurotransmitters in the synapses","explanation":"Serotonin syndrome arises from excessive serotonergic activity, especially synaptic serotonin accumulation or receptor overstimulation.","optionReasons":{"B":"Serotonin syndrome arises from excessive serotonergic activity, especially synaptic serotonin accumulation or receptor overstimulation."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a10fe0be5d73f92fedaa04c75169f0bf56c16f39db5ce184d9208e2327c9be07","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f5c75aa47740":{"correct":"B","answerText":"2-3 weeks","explanation":"Conventional antidepressant clinical response often becomes evident after two to four weeks; this is distinct from newer rapid-acting interventions.","optionReasons":{"B":"Conventional antidepressant clinical response often becomes evident after two to four weeks; this is distinct from newer rapid-acting interventions."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d34acbddc9155387cd2df8c3d774176a426720116fc0abd60049015d8b2137fb","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-cf672fdf0219":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Increase levels of biogenic amines","explanation":"Both monoamine oxidase inhibitors and tricyclic antidepressants generally enhance signaling by monoamine neurotransmitters.","optionReasons":{"C":"Both monoamine oxidase inhibitors and tricyclic antidepressants generally enhance signaling by monoamine neurotransmitters."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5ac1bda711a979670d6a618443b279fd51788dc1ebd20d6278e6aaaac73243bc","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-2daa734b1b2f":{"correct":"","answerText":"Recurrent laryngeal nerves, external branches of superior laryngeal nerves, parathyroid glands and their blood supply, trachea and major thyroid vessels.","explanation":"Recurrent laryngeal injury can cause vocal cord paresis; external superior laryngeal injury weakens pitch control. Parathyroid injury or devascularization can cause postoperative hypocalcemia.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ef98dc5f163c2a6a1e1e6a18d6147abb2394235740f5bcce4d9cdadf05b03075","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-de5cbf259bbf":{"correct":"","answerText":"Clavicle, sternal notch, coracoid process and the junction of the medial and middle thirds of the clavicle; use real-time ultrasound to identify the vein and pleura.","explanation":"Infraclavicular subclavian venous access follows the vein beneath the clavicle; the nearby subclavian artery, pleural apex and brachial plexus are major structures at risk. Ultrasound and sterile technique improve safety.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c38616f08b059f9169d55b1a3405a85152cb3cba3f31ca0c3932c6f4e23b8012","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-ad1d30b83a01":{"correct":"","answerText":"A right-sided subclavian approach may avoid the thoracic duct that joins the left venous angle.","explanation":"The thoracic duct terminates at the left jugulosubclavian junction, so injury and chylothorax are relatively more relevant to left-sided access; side selection must still account for anatomy, prior devices and complication risks.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e9994bdd9e1f29e4224dfc72d7fb78c0a2c1f4a4408a3105f6641a3139ac8f42","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-a346a704f3ad":{"correct":"","answerText":"Pelvic splanchnic nerves carry preganglionic parasympathetic fibers from S2–S4; most other splanchnic nerves carry sympathetic fibers.","explanation":"Pelvic splanchnics support bladder contraction, rectal motility and erectile vasodilation. Thoracic/lumbar/sacral sympathetic splanchnics arise from sympathetic pathways; the name does not imply a shared autonomic division.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4c295bf7a6674a09cc770e04e2a1870545a79c241dc853685f4f5cd1763fd009","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-a17975b8ffd4":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hypercapnia with respiratory acidosis; if prolonged, renal bicarbonate retention develops as compensation.","explanation":"Alveolar hypoventilation decreases carbon dioxide removal, increasing arterial PaCO2. The resulting carbonic acid lowers pH until renal bicarbonate generation partly compensates.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"273f40ebd2f23046a878a743015ec87f8eb0c404b5eabe02ab2c0418180cd5b4","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-55291c3eae0d":{"correct":"","answerText":"The cytochrome P450 enzyme system catalyzes many Phase I oxidation reactions, chiefly in liver microsomes, modifying drugs to more polar metabolites.","explanation":"CYP-mediated metabolism can inactivate, activate or toxify a drug and is a major source of pharmacokinetic interactions through enzyme induction and inhibition.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b5a132d4affa4ca41fbb721670d69c85ad565dc0e99bae58aef707b5874acfe5","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-fab29d97c89f":{"correct":"","answerText":"A buffer consists of a weak acid and its conjugate base, or a weak base and its conjugate acid.","explanation":"Buffers resist abrupt changes in pH by accepting or releasing hydrogen ions. Physiologic examples include bicarbonate/carbonic acid and phosphate buffer systems.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0145fcade59de323166cdcc1b0403900936ecb0750629745bb5d44989987193d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e1a61e5b3022":{"correct":"","answerText":"Four ATP molecules are produced gross per glucose during glycolysis.","explanation":"Two ATP are consumed in the investment phase and four are produced in the payoff phase; therefore the net yield is two ATP per molecule of glucose, including under anaerobic conditions.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9a7ea46921263933c092f0c54d03fc42016dbf0f67ab641bf4aaa0b3587c79d3","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-d74dc90132b6":{"correct":"","answerText":"To regenerate NAD+ from NADH so glycolysis can continue in the absence of adequate mitochondrial oxidation.","explanation":"Lactate dehydrogenase reduces pyruvate to lactate and oxidizes NADH to NAD+, sustaining the glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase reaction and anaerobic ATP production.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"23668211a37e6a7269444e8aa0ffccc940078a96045b1faa2a374ae2833f93f2","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-625fda5b0b76":{"correct":"","answerText":"Arachnoid mater.","explanation":"The arachnoid is a thin web-like meningeal layer between dura and pia; trabeculae extend through the CSF-filled subarachnoid space.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ede058f854d8f388ed138100e2826cc5e96f2b7fbd34c570174bdc9d06b530c5","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-cf035e26ba8f":{"correct":"","answerText":"Enterobius eggs are mainly deposited on perianal skin, while Strongyloides usually passes larvae rather than eggs in stool.","explanation":"A perianal adhesive-tape test is preferred for pinworm, whereas larval concentration, specialized stool examination or other targeted tests improve Strongyloides detection.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7b637ecdcd91dd9d683a3f8283b7215a88a441d1a19e872c0a1ea5a21db5b313","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-916b09e65605":{"correct":"","answerText":"Hepatitis A and hepatitis E generally cause acute, self-limited infections rather than chronic hepatitis in immunocompetent people.","explanation":"Hepatitis B, C and D may become chronic. Hepatitis E can persist in immunosuppressed people, so the usual statement requires that qualification.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0de678a7108b1a2051ff0684be9d2a75e970f1539f00fa281d5477e7e1241ad2","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-4e5d146b8334":{"correct":"","answerText":"Herpesviruses such as herpes simplex virus and varicella-zoster virus.","explanation":"Herpesviruses are enveloped double-stranded DNA viruses, unlike naked DNA viruses such as papillomaviruses and adenoviruses.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"82f4d4f2ec770c27724f171a74fdd5d7eccfb1657d03d094d4055abe4c16a1b2","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-b291d895c454":{"correct":"","answerText":"A typical nucleated cell expresses up to six different classical MHC class I molecules (two alleles each of HLA-A, -B and -C); a macrophage also expresses MHC class II (HLA-DP, -DQ and -DR, potentially multiple heterodimers).","explanation":"The exact number of unique class II proteins varies because several alpha/beta chains can pair; class I is expressed on most nucleated cells, whereas professional APCs express class II.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"317c7204997492627afe5ffe10b9b6b4fc18ba670cbc748aa58ff588f3a26d27","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-4ef2b4b89a26":{"correct":"","answerText":"Endogenous EBV proteins are degraded by proteasomes, loaded on MHC class I and recognized by CD8 T cells; phagocytosed or endocytosed viral proteins may be processed in endosomes and presented on MHC class II to CD4 T cells.","explanation":"EBV infects B lymphocytes, which are professional antigen-presenting cells. Cytosolic proteasome–TAP pathways generally support MHC I presentation and endosomal acid proteolysis supports MHC II presentation.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"195009d1a1969846f2388f07ed38cbea5bd7e75e92b7e0a49a2ca032c7f79581","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-3abd724ee7bf":{"correct":"","answerText":"Type I (immediate, IgE-mediated) hypersensitivity.","explanation":"Allergen cross-linking of mast-cell-bound IgE triggers histamine and other mediators, producing wheals and pruritus; non-IgE urticaria mechanisms also exist.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"cc86fd342b1a00cfc5b2feb7fa1a9bde20b7637bb2cfa9dc88ae10d9253a73ff","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-2147c88ee7cb":{"correct":"","answerText":"A primary immune response.","explanation":"On first antigen exposure, naive lymphocytes are activated; the early humoral response often begins with IgM before affinity maturation and class switching.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"59a7b2445350fd811cd445d9db471a781ab86c85b594023350c69eee3102f1d5","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-ba987737dc8b":{"correct":"","answerText":"Helper T cells are typically CD4-positive and recognize MHC II; cytotoxic T cells are typically CD8-positive and recognize MHC I.","explanation":"Helper T cells mainly coordinate immune responses via cytokines and costimulation; cytotoxic T cells kill infected or malignant target cells using perforin/granzymes or death receptors.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f2be5619cebeae6ad2bf896f3264a92ab63ec3a0fe13ab7f67fefa24aa3b8903","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f885ea404e51":{"correct":"","answerText":"Bacteria synthesize folate de novo from PABA; human cells obtain preformed folate from diet and lack the corresponding bacterial synthetic enzymes.","explanation":"Sulfonamides inhibit bacterial dihydropteroate synthase. This difference between bacterial and human folate acquisition creates selective toxicity, although adverse effects still occur.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"75c0fdaec939395f26e2295e8641191aa35d0304d159fb7f382bfa06a341f84d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-b41a59b709b3":{"correct":"","answerText":"Streptomyces species.","explanation":"This soil actinomycete genus produces numerous antibiotic classes as secondary metabolites, historically including streptomycin and tetracyclines.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0eeaea461c27e867834922b3f735f37dead5a66602f617adcffffafe601e103a","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0ed42e90b475":{"correct":"","answerText":"Primaquine and tafenoquine require quantitative G6PD testing because they can cause severe oxidant hemolysis in G6PD deficiency.","explanation":"8-aminoquinolines can trigger red-cell oxidative injury when NADPH-dependent defenses are impaired. Regimen choice depends on parasite species, G6PD status and guideline context.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"97dd7ff377999be16d21306f0930f4c1c9c9033ff47c4fb1774bf0e790d7d715","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-7b5ac51d1330":{"correct":"","answerText":"Combination antiretroviral therapy targets multiple stages of HIV replication to achieve durable viral suppression and reduce emergence of resistant variants.","explanation":"HIV reverse transcriptase is error prone and the virus replicates rapidly; using drugs with different targets makes it harder for a resistant clone to expand.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"2b8a16f07a8e4e38d5f97baf02bd120cbe30526e80249635cc29e945ef3d651e","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-3b52ad7a4224":{"correct":"","answerText":"Dicrocoelium dendriticum uses terrestrial snails and ants as intermediate hosts; unlike many flukes, its eggs do not require free-swimming aquatic stages.","explanation":"The snail releases parasite-containing slime balls that ants eat; infected ants can be ingested with pasture by herbivores, completing a land-based cycle.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"337f74f9987960bd8db1bb09f2b05966f4f828f11ffd5abebff6dd09bb856100","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-91490a8ecfaf":{"correct":"","answerText":"A paratenic host transports and harbors a parasite without essential development; an intermediate host supports a required developmental or asexual stage.","explanation":"Paratenic hosts are optional transport reservoirs while intermediate hosts are biologically needed for completion of the normal life cycle.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"669621a5248b3121662d4803281e58279c49601e222855f3428a8e9746cb9724","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0f0dece4ca2c":{"correct":"","answerText":"Echinococcus multilocularis produces infiltrative alveolar hydatid lesions that invade adjacent tissues and may disseminate; E. granulosus usually causes more expansile, cystic lesions.","explanation":"The multilocular growth pattern resembles malignancy, often affecting the liver with difficult surgical margins and prolonged anthelmintic therapy.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"06ec02f39191267c0cb8ab7d53fd80cfdc6e7a37b1468069a9f75aec11998431","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-2cd82a1a7508":{"correct":"","answerText":"Deposited schistosome eggs are the main drivers of chronic tissue inflammation and granulomatous pathology.","explanation":"Eggs lodged in intestinal or urinary tissues provoke eosinophilic granulomas and fibrosis; adult worms in vessels cause relatively less of the classical tissue injury.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6c7afb5d34e47970bbeb1cd2210c7c7de60361633b57a5c1454b6a43459963f0","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-29369ac1fe1d":{"correct":"","answerText":"Microscopy alone has imperfect sensitivity and cannot reliably distinguish E. histolytica from morphologically similar nonpathogenic species; intermittent cyst shedding also complicates detection.","explanation":"Species-specific antigen tests or PCR provide better discrimination, and multiple stool samples may improve the likelihood of detection.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9ce1091b7e5fb24d3d2dda4cbee273a03029315d46f4ef1dc35c24c5a86f55ed","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e1750dcbaa61":{"correct":"","answerText":"Giardia organisms are shed intermittently, so a single stool test can be falsely negative; cyst and trophozoite detection depends on specimen timing and technique.","explanation":"Repeat stool samples or antigen/PCR assays can improve diagnostic sensitivity compared with a one-time direct wet mount.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b8556ead407f6772215498b7916410caf1adf7273442ed4499593253455b1546","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-07977c20f119":{"correct":"","answerText":"Trichomonas vaginalis is transmitted directly as a motile trophozoite in a moist urogenital environment rather than through environmentally resistant fecal cysts.","explanation":"Its primarily sexual transmission does not require a dormant cyst stage; trophozoites are vulnerable to drying outside the host.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8bc07cc3df40d3f0604ab3e1514e05dbcdc492dd0f287a49137be86a8826adce","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-28c7cb038be0":{"correct":"","answerText":"A sigmoidal (S-shaped) oxygen–hemoglobin dissociation curve.","explanation":"Cooperative oxygen binding to the four heme sites changes hemoglobin affinity as oxygen saturation rises, producing the characteristic sigmoid shape.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"802fa963de7537805072165dcfe8813291838f652ece76dc49bac69a8754531e","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-eceb59f6c751":{"correct":"","answerText":"Common donor checks include identity and age eligibility, minimum weight, hemoglobin threshold, normal temperature/pulse/BP, and medical history screening for infection and risk exposures.","explanation":"Blood donation criteria protect both donors and recipients. Exact age, weight and hemoglobin thresholds depend on national transfusion service policies.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5084c63546549c26d6e50531c66f6f7800213d970cba40de80a4d1ac20fc3fa7","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-fd44281ef56a":{"correct":"","answerText":"The four main ABO blood groups are A, B, AB and O.","explanation":"ABO classification reflects A and B carbohydrate antigens on erythrocyte surfaces, with naturally occurring antibodies against absent antigens.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6fbe08ee2fa08f9d7a73b2a584de35ff3b5c7346d1df5a51c1a0ba75cd2d0ba7","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f480d6a63538":{"correct":"","answerText":"Sickle cell disease, typically homozygous hemoglobin SS (HbSS) when both inherited beta-globin genes encode hemoglobin S.","explanation":"Two sickle beta-globin alleles produce a disease phenotype with HbS polymerization during deoxygenation, hemolysis and vaso-occlusion.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"aecdd6abb54165de13b61e92a6a0eab39a04bf501726a91ccfcf2501e02dd336","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-eebb513ef3ec":{"correct":"","answerText":"Sickle cell trait (HbAS).","explanation":"Inheriting one beta-S allele and one normal beta-A allele produces the heterozygous carrier state, typically with much lower clinical risk than HbSS.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a40c0448f1645d29a43c7e3dce7a6c180d8e80f67dedccf56247865c493b600a","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-f7241ff8102c":{"correct":"","answerText":"Neutrophils, lymphocytes, monocytes, eosinophils and basophils.","explanation":"These five mature leukocyte categories comprise granulocytic and agranulocytic cells with complementary roles in innate and adaptive defense.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d1133892ded1ac85cc352a375c06abc6f1626eeb4e93d038d6080c85152c949d","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-0bb32ac613c2":{"correct":"","answerText":"Howell–Jolly bodies, Heinz bodies, Pappenheimer bodies and basophilic stippling.","explanation":"These are distinct erythrocyte inclusion findings: nuclear DNA remnants, denatured hemoglobin, iron-containing granules and ribosomal RNA aggregates respectively.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"14966357789e113036d7cf5e81fc600380c90513e2b1d37c070f257986083e31","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-96e06839de37":{"correct":"","answerText":"IgG, IgA, IgM, IgE and IgD.","explanation":"These are the five major immunoglobulin isotypes, defined by heavy-chain constant regions and different immune functions.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b7606e7fc146a09118b35588365970fe060128b094b5265512dbeb770379eb41","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e220aab849c3":{"correct":"","answerText":"Microcytosis, hypochromia, anisocytosis and poikilocytosis; pencil/elliptocyte forms may be present.","explanation":"Iron deficiency reduces hemoglobinization and cell size, causing low MCV and MCH with increased red-cell distribution width in established disease.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"2806f19ff21b12ee4b7606d831a20cd1b24cbc2e9211e4e6893c6dd4846f6f99","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-6656251db0d8":{"correct":"","answerText":"Macro-ovalocytes with anisopoikilocytosis and hypersegmented neutrophils.","explanation":"Vitamin B12 deficiency impairs DNA synthesis, producing megaloblastic maturation with nuclear–cytoplasmic asynchrony and large oval erythrocytes.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e4dcaa953f69114e290967ea4d275ddc2078e8bbc93b0dbc1c54f679e06d8979","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-e31836291aa1":{"correct":"","answerText":"Spherocytes.","explanation":"Loss of red-cell membrane surface area creates spherical erythrocytes with reduced central pallor in both inherited membrane defects and warm autoimmune hemolysis.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6718700e4d28816682e0e67359d4b64e264137eb3ffd0ea93b53784ddf2d6abc","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-1d8e00f81699":{"correct":"","answerText":"BCR–ABL1 fusion gene caused by t(9;22), the Philadelphia chromosome.","explanation":"This translocation produces a constitutively active tyrosine kinase driving chronic myeloid leukemia and providing a diagnostic and therapeutic molecular target.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"993ba0b1cc2b2e0fe98b029919ab6b5b3fd9ea98cd75d34d22581c61f4cf9885","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-b66c259153b1":{"correct":"","answerText":"ABO.","explanation":"The ABO blood group system was the first human red-cell antigen system identified, classically by Karl Landsteiner.","optionReasons":{},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1816b5f506f2164ac23d6c1b0a93150a84275f22f571d168d1b2b24d0197a868","answerFormat":"written_model"},"q-cd7634262dee":{"correct":"D","answerText":"GALT","explanation":"GALT means gut-associated lymphoid tissue, part of mucosal immune defenses.","optionReasons":{"D":"GALT means gut-associated lymphoid tissue, part of mucosal immune defenses."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bd4806415ccf1ebb8fd7fbbe2600d0ba6c9d881ba7d6385e13242d603fc3a525","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-e163f14b83c2":{"correct":"A","answerText":"BALT","explanation":"BALT denotes bronchus-associated lymphoid tissue in the airway mucosa.","optionReasons":{"A":"BALT denotes bronchus-associated lymphoid tissue in the airway mucosa."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e502a297abd3f8b7a3b5985ed22dc79305f0c16f360e024abfba328fdf5ef38b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-7a155e702a9a":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Outer cortex","explanation":"Outer cortex is the lymph-node follicular zone; the other terms describe deep cortex/paracortex.","optionReasons":{"C":"Outer cortex is the lymph-node follicular zone; the other terms describe deep cortex/paracortex."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a44c4009648a4fa317a879b75bfaddcd3ed3d84e5262a824c4fa17c0c29251b5","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-fb57b5be81d7":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Rapacuronium","explanation":"Rapacuronium was an unusually rapid-onset nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocker, although it was withdrawn because of severe bronchospasm risk.","optionReasons":{"B":"Rapacuronium was an unusually rapid-onset nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocker, although it was withdrawn because of severe bronchospasm risk."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f3fca386cb891154104625f235c40562ccb4bbc411ec74582c73a4c1f229444b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-bd6e2f45da15":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Tramadol","explanation":"Tramadol combines relatively weak mu-opioid receptor agonism with inhibition of norepinephrine and serotonin reuptake, accounting for mixed opioid and nonopioid mechanisms.","optionReasons":{"B":"Tramadol combines relatively weak mu-opioid receptor agonism with inhibition of norepinephrine and serotonin reuptake, accounting for mixed opioid and nonopioid mechanisms."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0d4d6312f849bd360e6722a7d9f344b16acd4330ffe55ded5eab83190dc500b7","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-81d41dcd0126":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Hyperactive dopaminergic state in the presence of dopamine blockers","explanation":"Tardive dyskinesia is associated with dopamine-receptor supersensitivity and maladaptive basal-ganglia signaling after prolonged receptor blockade.","optionReasons":{"B":"Tardive dyskinesia is associated with dopamine-receptor supersensitivity and maladaptive basal-ganglia signaling after prolonged receptor blockade."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d1839f980225f018298d2e39c6e1aaf73d3a7b42036cdeee40a226e834b8f987","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-10228b16dcdd":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Nerves","explanation":"Nervi vasorum denotes the autonomic nerves supplying blood vessel walls and regulating smooth-muscle tone.","optionReasons":{"D":"Nervi vasorum denotes the autonomic nerves supplying blood vessel walls and regulating smooth-muscle tone."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"00bb9bad0a46dc22e14044d2861060f4d60412cc0181a89cc4efb9772e45b55c","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-0f73eb008206":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Rapacuronium","explanation":"Rapacuronium was an unusually rapid-onset nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocker, although it was withdrawn because of severe bronchospasm risk.","optionReasons":{"B":"Rapacuronium was an unusually rapid-onset nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocker, although it was withdrawn because of severe bronchospasm risk."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f3fca386cb891154104625f235c40562ccb4bbc411ec74582c73a4c1f229444b","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"},"q-f6ff453942c8":{"correct":"B","answerText":"anterior cardiac vein","explanation":"Anterior cardiac veins generally drain directly into the right atrium rather than through the coronary sinus.","optionReasons":{"B":"Anterior cardiac veins generally drain directly into the right atrium rather than through the coronary sinus."},"references":[],"review":"provisional_independent_reasoning; no legacy source keys consulted","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"394e2ac85759ae8d19253a0a96fe2258e42c90bddeae1b14f51d72e3a1f9f775","answerFormat":"single_best_answer"}}}